  "rows": [
    {
      "number": 232,
      "title": "Prepare native core closure with two finite model-acquisition epochs",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/232",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-batch41-native-core-closure-20261031",
      "head_sha": "458256013f56fc35fa61770d81f050f2481e6212",
      "base_ref": "main",
      "base_sha": "88bf8ab6987619e8d989299474c250f5f1625d97",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-31T12:52:37Z",
      "body": "Advance the native-reference core compile prerequisite with a bounded passive acquisition client and two explicit, immutable model-acquisition epochs. The client reuses whole-pinned transport and metadata providers, verifies every served checksum, reads resource controls before HTTP and retains owned-scope cleanup. Downloaded Maven code is not executed.\n\nThe current source passes all 190 named normal/optimized unit executions: 22 client, 28 transport, 13 privacy and 32 metadata cases per mode. Preserve all original client cases, four new models-02 cases and all 15 negative modes. Independent source review required a stronger mandatory-POM HTTP404 control; the complete unexecuted first candidate and HOLD remain retained. Corrected whole-PR accounting counts final source once against the original base, including all root helpers, rather than summing intermediate replacements over newly introduced files.\n\nThe original models-01 epoch completed 175 fixed requests for 34 POMs and one version-metadata file; 61 served checksums matched. Models-02 completed 90 additional fixed requests for 18 POMs: 70 HTTP200 and 20 optional HTTP404 responses; 34 served checksums matched. All original nine project declarations, dependency ranges and plugin/model contexts remain in scope. These are finite model inputs, not selected or mediated binary closure.\n\nRetain the original 405-file public packet unchanged, with its 176 metadata projections and 350 cookie replacements. A separate models-02 packet retains exact Maven payloads, 91 independently verified projected metadata files with 180 cookie replacements, raw unit streams, source captures, admission records, cleanup and every held attempt. Private originals remain retained. Preserve the complete first models-02 publication candidate and Git-filter HOLD: inherited text conversion would have changed five CRLF payloads. Corrected passive-byte attributes, actual filter checks and committed-blob readback are required before publishing the repaired packet. PGP signatures are unverified; same-origin checksum consistency is not publisher authentication.\n\nInclusive final source is 391 production / 897 authored lines, counting the 63-line generator, the complete single 40-line current projection component, the 33-line publication copier, CI, documentation and attributes. Public records distinguish immutable historical execution inputs from later approved CI changes. Implementation and evidence are committed separately; current hosted checks and exact committed-tree verification remain independent gates.\n\nKeep this PR DRAFT until context-sensitive parent/BOM/property/profile/relocation/range collection, selected binary/processor/plugin closure and acquired-code review permit the exact unmodified offline compile of all 378 main Java sources with a fresh output witness. This does not complete C01, native application parity, durable Rust UI/backend restart, capacity or fully Rust release qualification. Existing holds and human reservations remain preserved.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 148,
      "title": "test(parser): retain actual native AST captures and unresolved differences",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/148",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-batch19-construction-tools",
      "head_sha": "b578866d4eccdcf56f3cd0117a6cbed4c5ed5cd2",
      "base_ref": "main",
      "base_sha": "08d0fa3a94e42c198a4b1482e63c50f28d0f1ace",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-29T03:51:15Z",
      "body": "Prepare development-only observations using the original pinned SysML lexer/parser through its original empty-filesystem service factory and direct public Rust Arena dumps. Preserve structural property/alias/default inventories, reference descriptors without getter resolution, CST spans and diagnostics. No application runtime or fallback is added.\n\nRetain 135 archived inputs/outputs, cancellation/formatting failures, original 39-case and expanded 42-case captures, exact constructor/corpus versions and separately bound inspection recipes. Independent review prompted outer-whitespace counterexamples; the candidate fixes observed spans. Preliminary inspection retains 79 child-cache differences across 22 finite programs, assigned to existing P14 qualification.\n\nDRAFT: structural-path identity bindings and reference-text inspection are diagnostic tools, not a final acceptance comparator. Complete container/reference-type/default/cache/caller qualification, native Node20/source correspondence, UI and capacity remain open. Recorded Node18 and explicit metadata exclusions remain visible. Constructor candidate #147 is a separate draft; no full parity or merge eligibility is claimed.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 130,
      "title": "RR20: integrate bounded history with borrowed-summary UI callers",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/130",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-batch14-history-summary-joint",
      "head_sha": "87c69ce02a826f84d3c9530d215e20e268b2cfc6",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3ef-joint-snapshot",
      "base_sha": "06fc56aa6c45bb45bdc6ff575ac1c7eae553cc37",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-28T23:59:54Z",
      "body": "Combines the existing bounded model history with borrowed-summary navigation on the current E/F UI snapshot. A real browser counterexample on the preserved baseline performs a 65th undo and changes Revision6 to Revision5; this composition keeps the 64-entry boundary and restores the exact final export after redo. Dense ownership, literal numeric tokens, marker objects and transaction refusal/identity behavior remain covered.\n\nValidation: 151 Rust host tests (74 model +77 web), formatting, all-target Clippy, debug/release WASM and 18 successful actual UI recipes on each configuration. A retained inspector readiness failure was fixed by waiting for the real region instead of the loading heading; only its failed/unexecuted remainder reran for debug. All18 recipes reran after release artifact changed. Release WASM is 965797 bytes. Restored-state undo samples use 2 warmups+7 measurements: sparse25.6\u201328.9ms, dense117\u2013131.4ms. Debug dense605\u2013638ms is separately retained. No p95, native SysON speed ratio or general capacity claim.\n\nFresh 1000/4096-node \u00d764/256-commit profiles include36 host samples with separate allocation/live/RSS meanings. Independent source, artifact, rendered/AX and raw metric reviews passed. All424 lossless archive entries and ignored logs match committed Git blobs. Raw capture whitespace is preserved; authored-file diff checking passes. Three commits separate implementation, UI qualification and generated evidence;885 authored additions fit the900-line review budget.\n\nDRAFT ONLY: this targets the exact frozen review snapshot, never a merge destination. Main landing waits for the actual UI/model prerequisite and ownership closure. RR19 availability copy, expanded identifier text wall, dense navigation, whole-render admission, glyph/assistive/browser/capacity acceptance, fully Rust browser ownership and durable project reopen remain open. Full SysON feature parity stays NOT_ACCEPTED. Existing #111/#115/#124/#125 and owner holds remain preserved.\n\nEvidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR20/joint-batch14/.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 125,
      "title": "RR18b3f: Keep saved values readable with exact native full-text access",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/125",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3f-saved-values",
      "head_sha": "2a77339282d996af5eb41775db0b78efc5a6fd88",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3c23-joint-snapshot",
      "base_sha": "c22c5b5fa664afc91c2d2d238fd766a60ba2f71f",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-28T15:53:14Z",
      "body": "Large saved/read-only JSON values created a many-screen paragraph before the usable control. Keep at most 80 serialized UTF-8 bytes inline and provide a labelled native disclosure with selectable readonly JSON for longer values. All complete values still count toward existing helper limits; model/export authority and quotas remain unchanged.\n\nActual rendered boundary testing found the initial 128-byte policy still made compact wide text wrap to 7\u20138 lines. The corrected source reduces those same writable/readonly cases to 2 lines / 33.6 px and 5 lines / 102 px, with exact full-value keyboard selection and unchanged models. Original failures and earlier source passes remain historical.\n\nFresh final verification: 77 default Rust cases including 142 unchanged helper goldens, exact ASCII/NUL/UTF-8 thresholds, formatting, Clippy and release WASM; all 17 browser recipes at 320/1440. Actual readonly repaint/caret/scroll, document epochs, history, helper refusal and exact 853,145-byte downloads pass. Seven-sample disclosure observations span 25.1\u201328.6 ms; separate task maxima 246/239 ms are recorded without a universal timing veto. Every one of 450 packet files and 4,815 joint source bindings was independently checked against committed Git. Source budget: 44 production / 447 authored additions; evidence is separate.\n\nReadonly repaint qualification requires implemented RR18b3e #124 on exact joint 06fc56aa. Actual native Package comparison preserves the Rust manual-reimport versus native reload difference; it does not establish persistence or full SysON parity. Glyphs, wider AX/browser/device coverage and global renderer memory remain open. Review-only C22 base: do not merge snapshots. Actual main prerequisites and existing owner/integration gates remain required.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 124,
      "title": "RR18b3e: Bound navigation labels and preserve visible native focus",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/124",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3e-navigation-focus",
      "head_sha": "feef7324d7a56903327333b6b25d77958c7862ca",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3c23-joint-snapshot",
      "base_sha": "c22c5b5fa664afc91c2d2d238fd766a60ba2f71f",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-28T15:52:55Z",
      "body": "A 4,096-character model name produced a 2,698 px navigation button. Render it in two visual lines while preserving the complete accessible name, kind, selection and a usable full-name control. Repaint now preserves visible focus, backward selection and local scrolling for editable and readonly native controls while respecting deliberate page scrolling.\n\nQualified on exact E+F composition 06fc56aa with 77 fresh default Rust tests, formatting, Clippy, release WASM and 17 actual browser recipes at 320/1440. The row is now 80 px; final seven-sample selection ranges are 31.0\u201331.6 ms sparse and 214.7\u2013252.8 ms dense. Workload ranges replace the universal timing veto; no percentile or native speed ratio is claimed.\n\nActual SysON and Rust Package editing/full-name access were compared. Rust manual export/reimport is not native persistence parity. Glyphs, dense-tree virtualization, wider browsers/devices and global renderer memory remain open. Every one of the 450 packet files, 4,815 joint input bindings, ignored logs and historical failures was independently checked against committed Git. Conservative source budget: 59 production / 368 authored additions; evidence is a separate commit.\n\nReview-only frozen C22 base. Do not merge into the snapshot. Actual main prerequisites, existing explicit owner holds, model reconciliation and exact landing qualification still apply. Full feature acceptance remains open.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 121,
      "title": "RR18b3c2: Qualify actual scalar helper refusal and recovery",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/121",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3c2-helper-refusal",
      "head_sha": "4a1da2e99ef5288b1e6a53f8d52e618060c46673",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3c3-textarea-drafts",
      "base_sha": "e600d5a12b546d03308b31a4918c54c2044087f6",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T22:09:08Z",
      "body": "Exercise the actual aggregate helper-limit caller for producer #119 with required loader repair #120. Two separately admitted scalar actions create a 1,700,422-byte pending model with an inspector lower bound of 17,000,000 bytes. Real controls reach recovery, preserve the exact 850,389-byte committed download/CRLF, unrelated drafts and backward caret, cancel the staged field, retain undo/redo and permit font-event discard confirmation.\n\nThis PR changes no production code. The initial recipe, diagnostic-only continuation and sealed evidence are three scoped commits (248 authored lines). Original runs failed before ABI dispatch because of the pristine-CRLF quota bug; both failures, original recipe and actual diagnostic records remain. The original assertions and font-confirmation scenario are unchanged.\n\nAt 320/1440, the exact repaired joint candidate c22c5b5fa664afc91c2d2d238fd766a60ba2f71f passes all consuming assertions, two actual attribute requests and one import per viewport, native download/keyboard/AX/focus checks and fifteen distinct affected recipes. Producer WASM is reused explicitly with identical compiled inputs; no fresh child Rust build/test claim. Own source and external prerequisite composition are separately bound; independent review verifies all 180 committed packet files, sixteen lossless captures and 4,809 joint inputs.\n\nThe base is the required loader PR #120, which carries #119; this verification branch's own HEAD deliberately does not graft the loader. Retarget/requalify actual main after prerequisites land. Never merge feature/snapshot bases to simulate landing. Old EXPLICIT_ONLY holds and shared-model reconciliation remain required. Stress tasks 290/287 ms, saved-value walls, glyphs, total rendering and full parity remain open. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR18b3c2/.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 120,
      "title": "RR18b3c3: Preserve pristine CRLF textareas during draft admission",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/120",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3c3-textarea-drafts",
      "head_sha": "e600d5a12b546d03308b31a4918c54c2044087f6",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3c-bounded-helpers",
      "base_sha": "bad17e7090ca86cc886c695982894dc7d802e643",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T22:08:53Z",
      "body": "An unchanged CRLF textarea was charged as a dirty draft because native value is LF-normalized while defaultValue retains CR. With another large draft, this falsely exhausted the 1 MiB cache before any attribute request reached Rust. Actual failed diagnostics and a fresh old-loader regression retain the counterexample.\n\nSeventeen loader lines compare native textarea defaults with a no-copy UTF16 CRLF/CR-to-LF scan. Focused fields remain retained; true edits, clears, extra LF/Unicode differences, INPUT/SELECT/checked behavior, quotas and model bytes remain unchanged. No Rust, CSS or Cargo change. Two commits separate the 163-line authored repair/recipe/preparation and exact evidence.\n\nTwelve native cases at 320/1440 pass, including genuine quota refusals, real attribute staging, cancellation, dirty/cleared draft preservation and font/caret retention. The original 850k+850k helper consumer and fifteen distinct affected browser recipes pass on exact c22c5b5fa664afc91c2d2d238fd766a60ba2f71f. Qualified producer WASM is explicitly reused; no fresh Rust test/build claim. Independent review verifies all 180 committed packet files, sixteen lossless captures, own source and 4,809 joint inputs. The one repeated matrix invocation and textarea remainder are explicit.\n\nDepends on producer #119 for this reviewed stack; the separate RR18b3c2 consumer records its own prerequisite composition. Do not merge into feature/snapshot bases: actual main prerequisites, old EXPLICIT_ONLY holds and landing-tree qualification remain required. Stress tasks still reach 290/287 ms; total renderer admission, saved-value walls, glyphs, general visible focus and full SysON parity remain open. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR18b3c3/.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 119,
      "title": "RR18b3c: Count scalar and escaped HTML before allocating output",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/119",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3c-bounded-helpers",
      "head_sha": "bad17e7090ca86cc886c695982894dc7d802e643",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3ab-joint-snapshot",
      "base_sha": "acf6707ba4104e61d47639ecf088376e19a48f79",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T21:52:25Z",
      "body": "An accepted 700 KB opaque import requested 88,951,293 allocation bytes during actual dispatch. Counted escaping and complete scalar-inspector emission reduce the same window to 32,944,233 bytes while preserving canonical export and 3,504,258 HTML bytes. Largest request remains 7,006,834; this measures allocation traffic, not RSS or a global bound.\n\nThe immutable count/emit sink streams JSON through existing authority, rejects before output reservation, preserves 142 frozen legacy helper outputs, and propagates failures through actual preview/navigation/recovery callers. Sticky errors also reject swallowed writer failures. Existing owned inspection remains and adds a model-size scan; complete HTML/navigation/options/SVG/export/geometry construction and required <50 ms remain open.\n\nFresh verification: 72 default web cases, scoped formatting, all-target Clippy, fresh release WASM cd252878 and thirteen actual browser recipes covering native scalar/AX/keyboard/history/drafts/canvas/downloads. Direct prepared oversized helpers request zero output allocation. Final source and all 174 committed packet files (4,804 input bindings; 20 lossless captures) were independently reviewed. Two commits separate implementation and evidence.\n\nA separate actual consumer exposed a pristine-CRLF draft-quota bug before ABI dispatch. Required RR18b3c2 consumer and RR18b3c3 loader repair retain those failures and qualify their exact composition separately; no helper-error consumer pass is inferred from that timeout. Global performance, saved-value walls, glyphs, visible focus and native SysON comparison remain open.\n\nReview-only frozen a+b base acf6707ba4104e61d47639ecf088376e19a48f79. Do not merge into the snapshot. Actual main prerequisites, old EXPLICIT_ONLY holds, RR20/shared-model reconciliation and exact landing-tree checks remain required. Scope: conservative 400 production additions / 876 authored lines; source/evidence in porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR18b3c/.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 116,
      "title": "RR18b3b: Reduce native textarea layout with literal local scrolling",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/116",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3b-textarea-layout",
      "head_sha": "556f17332c32512df61980afd68c065e4f22ddfd",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b-joint-snapshot",
      "base_sha": "40b3c1b3e6d86fb9ba082864dda4d17e6be8ee5b",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T19:59:09Z",
      "body": "Large literal JSON and rename textareas repeatedly soft-wrapped long lines in native browser layout. Eleven scoped CSS lines preserve exact whitespace and use local scrolling in four JSON controls plus the rename field. No Rust, loader, scalar, font or visibility shortcut is changed.\n\nActual 320/1440 checks pass LF/CRLF/tab/Unicode values, unchanged CRLF model submission, native keyboard selection/scroll, backward caret, focus styling, AX names/values/multiline/readonly, edit/history and draft recovery. Four focused/trace/ordinary/identity scripts plus six affected regression recipes pass. Exact joint a+b passes eleven recipes.\n\nOn the named CDP trace, Layout maxima fall from 86.880/47.513 ms to isolated 25.960/25.287 ms (joint 26.376/25.117 ms). These are individual observations, not a latency guarantee. Joint phase tasks still reach 62/61 ms and ordinary recovery 94/104 ms; required <50 ms acceptance remains OPEN. Visual review also found inherited missing glyphs, oversized navigation labels and offscreen focused controls; RR18b3d/e track them explicitly.\n\nQualified unchanged base WASM is reused for CSS-only checks; no fresh Rust build/test is claimed. Joint separately uses A's fresh WASM and 124 qualified Rust cases. Independent review verifies all 4,788 source bindings and all 198 committed packet files including the seal. Three commits separate CSS/meaningful browser recipe, evidence, and exact ignored-log publication repair. Original empty-AX oracle failure is retained; the correction permits omission only for an actually empty DOM field. Synthetic evidence privacy review passed.\n\nReview prerequisite: snapshot 40b3c1b3e6d86fb9ba082864dda4d17e6be8ee5b. Do not merge into this temporary snapshot; retarget only after main prerequisites/owner gates and landing-tree qualification. No full HTML, broad usability or SysON parity acceptance.\n\nSee porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR18b3b/RESULTS.md, PERFORMANCE-SCENARIOS.json and SHA256.json.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 115,
      "title": "RR18b3a: Borrow renderer summaries without owner-string amplification",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/115",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b3a-borrowed-summaries",
      "head_sha": "80eafc44f56555f31d8ff258ca0a87c3ee40fa3a",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b-joint-snapshot",
      "base_sha": "40b3c1b3e6d86fb9ba082864dda4d17e6be8ee5b",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T19:59:05Z",
      "body": "A 192,234-byte document with a long owner ID caused repeated summary-string copies during actual import/render. This adds borrowed read-only element summaries backed by the existing traversal and adopts them in the renderer/navigation. The same measured ABI window falls from 98,945,638 to 31,268,710 requested allocation bytes; exact model export and HTML size remain unchanged. This measures allocation traffic, not RSS or a global bound.\n\n124 default Rust cases (62 model + 62 web), scoped formatting, Clippy and fresh release WASM pass. Actual desktop/mobile dense ownership, selection/edit/history, recovery, canvas and download journeys pass. Eleven recipes pass on exact a+b candidate acf6707ba4104e61d47639ecf088376e19a48f79. Independent review verifies all 4,795 source bindings and all 166 committed packet files including the seal; large raw captures are losslessly compressed.\n\nThree scoped commits preserve implementation, evidence and the correction that explicitly adds ignored sealed HTTP logs. A test-only disclosure visibility correction retains the failed original recipe and avoids replaying unchanged Rust checks. Outgoing evidence was audited: synthetic localhost inputs/screenshots only, HTTP logs contain static GET/status lines, no credentials.\n\nReview prerequisite: exact joint snapshot 40b3c1b3e6d86fb9ba082864dda4d17e6be8ee5b. Do not merge into this snapshot branch. Main landing requires actual prerequisites, held-owner gates, RR20/shared-model reconciliation and affected landing-tree verification. The source author prepared the adapter under root grant; root owns serialized shared-file integration and exports.\n\nFull HTML/helper/geometry admission, other owned-summary consumers, <50 ms responsiveness, glyph coverage and navigation/visible-focus usability remain RR18b3c/d/e. Dense joint tasks reach 165/178 ms; no whole-UI or SysON parity acceptance is claimed.\n\nSee porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR18b3a/RESULTS.md, PERFORMANCE-SCENARIOS.json, CAPTURE-MANIFEST.json and SHA256.json.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 114,
      "title": "RR18b2: Preserve bounded recovery drafts without trapping document actions",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/114",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b2-recovery-drafts",
      "head_sha": "592e918c892fcdef8439fea9056c41da3599013f",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr18-preview-recovery",
      "base_sha": "b304b6df8711062cece3e2a557a3f73d3f9dc462",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T20:44:04Z",
      "body": "Artifact clarification (batch11): this historical head omits twelve HTTP logs listed in its seal. [Merged #117](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/117) publishes their exact retained bytes as a declared supplement. Source bindings remain valid, but the original head is not directly self-contained; use the supplement explicitly. Historical heads/seals are unchanged. This corrects any earlier blanket committed-packet claim; no runtime replay or source change is implied.\n\nRecovery could lose unrelated creation/import/geometry drafts. This adds bounded presentation-only retention with exact document/selection scope, focus/caret and disclosure restoration. Quota refusal keeps the connected DOM; acknowledged import/confirmed discard clears old contexts. Mandatory cancellation now suppresses stale canvas callbacks even when draft quota blocks dispatch.\n\nIndependent review also found a real UI deadlock: selecting a valid long imported element ID blocked later actions. A focused second source commit charges full exact inspector identity only when needed, preserves native disclosure defaults, and provides mutable document-level quota escapes. No model JSON copy/hash, semantic engine or asynchronous request queue is added.\n\nPrerequisite: exact RR18a #112 at b304b6df8711062cece3e2a557a3f73d3f9dc462. Three commits preserve initial implementation, the independently found long-ID correction, and sealed evidence. Only loader.js is production code. No held raw/graph/factory features, merge or deployment. Land prerequisites, retarget and requalify.\n\nVerification: final-source actual browser runs pass six long-ID cases (214/200014/600014 characters at 320/1440 widths), twelve cache guards, recovery/Keep/confirm, the callback race and both encoding/decoding faults. Ordinary uninstrumented recovery preserves model/canvas/history/drafts and downloads exact 900381-byte JSON / 2701179-byte URI; keyboard, identity, console and screenshots are checked. Nine scripts pass on the exact corrected B1+B2 candidate 40b3c1b3e6d86fb9ba082864dda4d17e6be8ee5b. Qualified unchanged Rust WASM is explicitly reused; no fresh Rust tests/build are claimed. Independent review covers 330 sealed files, 4706 isolated and 4786 separate joint bindings.\n\nOriginal failures, prior-source passes, surrogate oracle correction, newline timeout and long-ID near-budget setup correction are retained with exact attribution. Final joint phase observations are 105/70 ms and canvas 108/67 ms: required <50 ms acceptance remains OPEN in RR18b3. Cache bounds do not bound full HTML/DOM work, heap/RSS or broad usability. Missing CJK glyph coverage and other UI polish remain explicit tasks. No complete SysON parity claim.\n\nSee porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR18b2/RESULTS.md, PERFORMANCE-SCENARIOS.json and SHA256.json.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 113,
      "title": "RR18b1: Bound canvas transport before output allocation",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/113",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr18b1-canvas-transport",
      "head_sha": "7f1ae8f4e6b618b75615f589f35ce25f79600efb",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr18-preview-recovery",
      "base_sha": "b304b6df8711062cece3e2a557a3f73d3f9dc462",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T20:43:54Z",
      "body": "Artifact clarification (batch11): this historical head omits four HTTP logs listed in its seal. [Merged #117](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/117) publishes their exact retained bytes as a declared supplement. Source bindings remain valid, but the original head is not directly self-contained; use the supplement explicitly. Historical heads/seals are unchanged. This corrects any earlier blanket committed-packet claim; no runtime replay or source change is implied.\n\nOversized canvas JSON was rejected only after building large outputs: the actual baseline apply allocated 2,097,152 bytes in one request before refusal. This counts borrowed geometry and its JSON-string-wrapped ABI envelope before reserving output, preserves exact legacy wire bytes, shares immutable admitted frame buffers, and compares canonical model bytes without owning another model-sized string. Known committed-model actions no longer serialize before/after every dispatch.\n\nPrerequisite: exact RR18a #112 at b304b6df8711062cece3e2a557a3f73d3f9dc462. Two commits separate implementation and sealed evidence. No Cargo/registry changes, held raw/graph/factory features, merge or deployment. Land prerequisites, retarget and requalify.\n\nVerification: 60 default Rust cases, scoped formatting, all-target Clippy and fresh release WASM pass. The reproduced refusal now passes with no allocation request above 65,536 bytes in its measured apply window, preserving prior canvas/history. Desktop/mobile actual controls verify layout/compute/apply, rotation, history, geometry import, model staging/commit and refusal; ordinary uninstrumented RR18a recovery/download/keyboard and identity checks pass. One browser locator failure is retained and corrected without replaying unchanged Rust suites. Independent source/evidence review covers 91 seals and 4,696 input bindings.\n\nThis is the foundation child of RR18b, split before mutation. Full HTML/helper allocation, draft-cache composition and required <50 ms whole-task acceptance remain RR18b3. Individual instrumented task observations are 106/65 ms versus baseline 111/69 ms, not a statistical improvement or accepted latency budget. External phase-fixture current hash/provenance and the historical missing per-epoch fixture guard are explicitly documented. Requests still allocate a bounded canonical key; wire caches can increase retained memory; explicit exports own a copy. No whole-app memory or full SysON parity claim.\n\nSee porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR18b1/RESULTS.md and SHA256.json.\n\nComposition follow-up: [RR18b2 #114](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/114) adds bounded recovery drafts and the independently found long-ID repair. Nine actual browser scripts pass on exact composed candidate 40b3c1b3e6d86fb9ba082864dda4d17e6be8ee5b. This separate integration evidence is sealed in #114; full HTML and required <50 ms acceptance remain OPEN in RR18b3.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 112,
      "title": "RR18a: Preserve editor state on preview refusal and keep recovery reachable",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/112",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr18-preview-recovery",
      "head_sha": "b304b6df8711062cece3e2a557a3f73d3f9dc462",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr-batch9-base",
      "base_sha": "b1951bbaf15a1abcfb855702dc06f4230fb5263b",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T16:48:21Z",
      "body": "A valid 700,258-byte escaped-name import replaced the live editor and cleared history before the preview exceeded 16 MiB, leaving only an ineffective Undo control. Import now admits a private candidate with the exact final presentation and next canvas identity before replacing state. Recovery provides a byte-exact committed-model download, recover and confirmed discard/keep actions; absent canvas frames skip model serialization. A narrow loader fix preserves the focused textarea caret after refused import.\n\nThis is the first child of RR18, split before source mutation. Full before-allocation HTML/geometry rendering and generic fallback draft caching remain RR18b. Snapshot base b1951bbaf15a1abcfb855702dc06f4230fb5263b pins RR04 #94 and exact #65 UI/layout dependencies; provenance and root-owned lock wiring are recorded. Land prerequisites, retarget and requalify rather than merging the snapshot base as integration. RR18a does not consume evolving RR20. Active raw/graph/factory holds remain unchanged and disabled.\n\nVerification: 53 unique default Rust cases, final all-target Clippy and a fresh default release WASM build. Two test-helper Clippy failures are preserved; 47 unchanged library passes are retained, five affected ABI cases and one private URI case are requalified on their final helpers. Exact source-hash reconstruction proves production stayed unchanged.\n\nActual Chromium at 320/1440 widths verifies malformed/oversized import preserves model, canvas, undo/redo, drafts, focus and backward caret; native keyboard download, recover, keep and confirmed discard pass. Both 900,381-byte downloads equal committed JSON exactly; their URI is 2,701,179 bytes. No console warnings/errors, page errors or horizontal overflow. Supplemental title/URL/nonblank/overlay checks pass. Source/evidence independently reviewed: 89 seals and 4,610 input bindings. Two commits separate implementation and evidence; see porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR18a/RESULTS.md.\n\nThe journey records long tasks up to 111/71 ms. RR18b now has these exact fixtures and a required <50 ms task budget on the pinned reference profile; responsiveness acceptance remains OPEN. Normal HTML still materializes before its cap. Parent RR18, RR19, broader UI/usability/performance and full SysON parity remain OPEN. Nothing merged or deployed.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 111,
      "title": "RR20: Bound retained model undo and redo history",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/111",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr20-history-budgets",
      "head_sha": "fa75a22dbfa7fc9e0fc63c427df0d8f4b673035a",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr-batch9-base",
      "base_sha": "b1951bbaf15a1abcfb855702dc06f4230fb5263b",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T16:37:34Z",
      "body": "Repeated edits retained every whole-document snapshot. This adds a combined maximum of 64 undo/redo entries and a 128 MiB conservative capacity charge, deterministic eviction, typed availability/truncation, exact numeric-token preservation and refusal before revision exhaustion changes state. Commits preserve current data even when a prior snapshot cannot be retained.\n\nPrerequisites are frozen RR04 #94 and exact #65 UI/layout inputs in `porting/rust-parity-prerequisites/BATCH9/source-manifest.json`. The snapshot base is for review: land prerequisites, retarget and requalify; do not merge the snapshot as an integration branch. No held raw/factory/graph feature is enabled. Two focused commits separate implementation and sealed evidence.\n\nVerification: 70 model and 44 web tests, both default all-target Clippy gates, scoped formatting and a fresh release WASM build pass. Desktop/mobile Chromium exercises 70 real rendered edits, 64 keyboard undos and 64 redos per viewport with exact exports, no errors/overflow or observed long tasks. Independent source/evidence review checks 94 seals and 4,606 tested input bindings against head fa75a22dbfa7fc9e0fc63c427df0d8f4b673035a. Original counterexample and failed fixture attribution are retained.\n\nThe identical host probe measures all four 1000/4096-node \u00d7 64/256-edit profiles. In the largest case, requested retained live allocations fall from 1,500,287,745 to 58,377,296 bytes; process RSS after edits falls from 1,700,348 to 95,808 KiB. These are single-process observations, not an RSS guarantee or native SysON comparison. Conservative byte charging retains 40/9 steps in these larger fixtures, below the 64-entry maximum. Begin/apply copy costs remain unchanged.\n\nSee `porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR20/RESULTS.md` and `SHA256.json`. RR19 visible truncation/disabled controls, large rendered workloads, transaction-copy optimization, full integration and feature-parity acceptance remain OPEN. Nothing is merged or deployed.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 110,
      "title": "Bind selected integration receipts to committed source inventories (RR16a)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/110",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr16a-receipt-closure",
      "head_sha": "06ad70431b30d37729c19540ef59270288e39eb8",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-split-s18-20261024",
      "base_sha": "af4587008df81a3c16ab15fcb5b799a6f0d7438c",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T15:28:59Z",
      "body": "The old integration checkpoint emitted generic PASS for a fixed seven-command list or a resumed suffix, omitted consumed tool/backend/porting inputs, and never checked source afterward. Replace it with explicit admission, dynamic candidate Cargo inventory, full committed-repository input superset, Git byte/mode/type checks, declared historical/external/tool pins and before/after seals for every selected command. Resume and unsupported/held scopes stay explicit; this foundation never emits full qualification.\n\nVerification: 25 owned Git/Python-stub mechanism cases pass. Four original counterexamples and an exit7 positive control are retained. After an initial22-case pass, review found tree-listing/tree-revision/tree-HEAD authority gaps; all three freshly fail on that exact passed source before minimal commit/blob guards are added and the full25 suite is requalified. The timeout case records a same-group descendant's PID/start/group and checks termination before its natural exit; direct leader is reaped. Synthetic stub output is not a Rust parity result.\n\nThe reviewed implementation is committed before a real safe qualification: pinned Ecore generator --check plus dependency-free default metamodel tests. Both commands pass, with11actual Rust cases,15manifest inventory and4171tracked candidate inputs sealed unchanged per command/finally. The receipt is SELECTED_CHECKS_PASSED/full_qualification=false. Exact real tool identities and fresh workspace Cargo home/target/scratch are declared. No held graph/factory/raw code executes. Independent source/evidence audit, exact bindings and failure retention pass.\n\nTwo commits separate producer/tests/preparation and evidence. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR16a/RESULTS.md. CLI now requires --admission; old implicit invocations refuse. Code is based on exact #19 af4587008df81a3c16ab15fcb5b799a6f0d7438c; actual qualification targets implementationa32fdc5b793ccd1edce454864991f5b017db432f, and publication adds evidence only. Retarget/requalify after prerequisites; never merge into the feature base. RR16b consumes RR16a and joint RR23 #109 for full composed qualification after owner admission; parent RR16/RR17 remain OPEN. Explicit declarations do not prove arbitrary dynamic/registry/sysroot/toolchain completeness or hostile transient mutation. Native/UI/usability/performance/capacity/full parity, historical holds and canonical dirty work remain unchanged. No merge/deploy.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 109,
      "title": "Qualify the four repaired readers together on one Rust candidate (RR23)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/109",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr23-joint-integration",
      "head_sha": "313949a9c84a2997703c02b8a69072e24ad9f5dd",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr23-joint-base",
      "base_sha": "979c7742f8e5d6d4f02959143612c2ea82a13930",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T15:04:19Z",
      "body": "The four observed-contract readers previously had separate qualification trees. Compose their exact reviewed sources on one candidate and add an evidence-only Rust consumer linking all four libraries and the shared literal authority into a single process. Preserve every provider/capture/query byte and each reader's distinct typed-number policy.\n\nFresh verification on that composition passes 108 tests (19 GraphQL,20 DB,24 HTTP,23 templates,16 shared literal,6 joint consumer), all six Clippy/build gates, formatting and 30 actual CLI families. The joint caller uses manual marker maps/raw numeric oracles; CLI comparison distinguishes numeric tokens from strings and compares complete native captures. Actual errors stay errors, failed template observations remain unselectable, empty pages remain successful, and nine HTML frontend shells are not relabeled API successes. All44 donor/oracle inputs and before/after52 input maps bind exactly; independent source/evidence audit passes.\n\nTwo commits separate the joint consumer/recipe from exact qualification evidence. After execution only one preparation sentence was corrected: hashing precedes commands; runner copy is retained in finally. The documentation-only continuation has zero commands and retains exact original document bytes. Six test-output EOF blank lines remain verbatim hash-bound evidence, outside authored whitespace checks. No test result is relabeled onto changed code.\n\nBase979c7742f8e5d6d4f02959143612c2ea82a13930 is commonad814 plus43 executable-source grafts and one historical DB oracle from exact #105/#106/#107/#108 and common #100. Prerequisite provenance records every Git blob/mode/SHA256; no provider production changes or new registry tuple. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR23/RESULTS.md. Land prerequisite PRs, retarget and requalify; never merge into the temporary composition base. This closes selected joint literal-reader qualification only. C01/source-artifact, application/API/runtime/UI/usability/performance/capacity and full feature acceptance remain OPEN. Historical holds/canonical dirty work unchanged; no native epoch, merge or deploy.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 108,
