      "base_sha": "67ce68d5a8a20c913b21eba901484d1f101944f3",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T13:59:46Z",
      "body": "The HTTP observation reader could reinterpret marker-named objects and change numeric spelling. Adopt the qualified shared LastWins literal authority for mappings, probes and the fixed manifest, then move admitted captures directly into report metadata. Preserve existing decoded key/string/aggregate guards and the original typed body_bytes:-0 acceptance without changing captured tokens.\n\nVerification: 24 unique tests pass (11 inherited, 13 new), covering both readers, manual marker/token oracles, typed refusals and exact physical/depth/raw/decoded bounds. The initial full suite passes before Clippy flags a new test-only owned comparison; only that affected assertion/test is changed and requalified, with identical production. Final Clippy/format/build and independent source review pass. Eight actual CLI cases preserve the complete 54-handler/33-MVC mapping and 22 probe captures, fixed manifest bytes, both raw literal lanes, negative-zero compatibility and typed refusals. Nine status200 HTML shells remain frontend observations, not API successes.\n\nOriginal AP-only baseline has four passes/four failures; explicit dependency feature unification enables RawValue behavior and has two passes/six failures. First-token red reachability is recorded separately from final numeric-loop coverage. New physical-before-collapse/root-depth/scalar limits deliberately tighten old collapsed/default admission while retaining existing decoded limits. No global allocation/latency claim.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and exact evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR23c/RESULTS.md. Base 67ce68d5a8a20c913b21eba901484d1f101944f3 preserves exact #83 plus six unchanged qualified #100 crate blobs; #90/#100 remain required. Root owns Cargo wiring and serial offline execution. Land prerequisites, retarget/requalify; never merge into the snapshot. Original main/file-admission/captures and historical holds remain unchanged. Parent RR23 joint integration, C01, native/UI/performance/full-feature acceptance remain OPEN. No new registry tuple, native epoch, merge or deploy.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
