      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T13:28:49Z",
      "body": "The database observation reader could reinterpret marker objects as valid typed descriptors under composed serde_json features. Adopt qualified shared LastWins literal admission and retain the original signed-integer refusal of negative zero with a borrowed numeric token check. SQL/default/comment strings, strict descriptor/integrity rules, comparison policy and native captures remain unchanged.\n\nVerification: 20 tests pass on final production. Manual marker objects refuse in typed slots; canonical integer extremes and opaque strings survive. A type-correct public fixture accepts exactly2M independently counted physical values in4,058,405raw bytes; one overwritten extra value refuses. Exact depth128/129 and8MiB/+1 controls run. Four actual final CLI cases reproduce the full historical native projection (164 descriptors/20 ordered migrations) and three typed refusals without stdout. Original standalone default configuration passes all five controls; explicit feature-unified baseline has two passes/three failures. Root's omitted owned-fixture environment variable and a later Clippy owned-comparison failure remain preserved. After the production optimization, all affected tests/Clippy/build/CLI are freshly requalified. Independent review and exact committed-input bindings pass.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR23b/RESULTS.md. Snapshot f6f794697aaa572fdfac20018afb87261fc7f6ef preserves exact #79 plus six qualified #100 crate blobs, with #90/#100 required. Physical admission deliberately tightens old collapsed/default bounds. Land dependencies, retarget/requalify; never merge into the snapshot. No fresh DB/native epoch, PostgreSQL capacity/global allocation/timing, schema equivalence, UI or parent RR23/C01/full parity acceptance, held-path edit, registry expansion, merge or deployment.",
      "labels": []
