      "base_sha": "d481f79e4722163aa31c90956f036fc33f66ceea",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T13:28:46Z",
      "body": "The observed GraphQL reader could reinterpret marker-named schema objects under composed serde_json features and normalize numeric spellings. Use the qualified shared LastWins literal authority, then insert the admitted schema directly into the report to avoid generic Value reserialization. Keep typed metadata validation, array order, query/capability bytes and all native captures unchanged.\n\nVerification: 19 unique tests pass (10 inherited, nine new), including manual marker maps, -0/decimal/exponent/4096-digit tokens, typed refusals, duplicates, exact32MiB/depth128/2M physical-value boundaries and one-over controls. Five actual CLI cases preserve the full native selected schema (671 types/3148 members), query/capability bytes, BadFaith refusal, and independent raw marker/numeric payloads. Original-default baseline passes both marker controls but fails first numeric -0; feature-unified baseline fails all three. These are distinct configurations, with later numeric subcases first reached in final green. Initial full tests pass then Clippy flags a new test helper; its exact test-only fix is requalified without replaying unrelated passed tests. All-target Clippy, formatting, independent review and source bindings pass.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR23a/RESULTS.md. Snapshot d481f79e4722163aa31c90956f036fc33f66ceea preserves exact #80 plus six qualified #100 crate blobs; #90/#100 prerequisites remain required. LastWins preserves duplicate compatibility, with explicit physical/depth/scalar admission tightening. Land prerequisites, retarget/requalify; never merge into the snapshot. RR23b/c/d and parent RR23/C01 remain separate gates. No fresh native epoch, runtime/resolver/UI/full parity claim, held-path change, registry expansion, merge or deploy.",
      "labels": []
