      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T13:28:41Z",
      "body": "Project preparation still generically deserialized payload JSON: semantic preflight could reject a valid marker-named object, and representation staging could reinterpret it. Adopt the qualified shared LastWins literal authority for preflight and materialization, preserving the existing ordered namespace carrier, strict model API, migration order, six independent stamps, IDs and wire envelope.\n\nVerification: 85 cases pass on the exact composition (44 migrations, 11 pipeline, 17 preparation, 11 wire, plus both explicitly selected RR22 caller gates). Seven new preparation cases and one wire case use manual marker/numeric oracles through actual prepare/encode/decode/reprepare, exact bounds, late failures and unchanged previous output. Both named caller gates that failed under #103 now pass; the newer model prerequisite may already improve the inherited semantic gate, so RR22 also retains two distinct fresh preparation counterexamples on this composed base. Scoped formatting, all four Clippy gates, independent source review and committed-input bindings pass.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and exact evidence. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR22/RESULTS.md. Snapshot 203d9bc19b23e3453ce9d7a28b9d962b4cbb0468 preserves exact #103 plus five unchanged latest #94 model files (including #91 literal adoption); qualified #100 source remains pinned. Root alone owns manifests/four locks and serialized offline execution. Land prerequisites, retarget and requalify; never merge into the snapshot. Physical-before-collapse limits deliberately tighten old collapsed admission. No cancellation/latency/global-allocation/durable-publication guarantee, held-path edit, new registry tuple, native/UI/feature acceptance, merge or deployment.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
