      "base_sha": "1c3dbf782ccfc3884f95c7c7ed9019b1e613135b",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T03:29:15Z",
      "body": "Generic Value parsing could reinterpret marker-named objects and normalize numbers in shared migration support and B25d. Adopt qualified [RR24a #100](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/100) once, inspect the ordered literal namespace before materialization, and remove both old generic visitors. Preserve first-position/final-value duplicate semantics, participant/removal order, raw/token identity, stamps, replay/foreign behavior and private failure staging. Explicit input admission counts physical overwritten values/keys before collapse; byte/depth conventions and conservative scalar budget are documented.\n\nVerification: four immutable baseline tests fail on reached marker/numeric/namespace assertions; early failures skip later loop subcases, which are not claimed separate red measurements. Final green reaches all subcases. All 64 ordinary cases pass (44 migration including eight new, ten preparation, ten wire including doctest), scoped formatting and all three Clippy gates. Actual ordinary prepare/encode/decode/reprepare preserves six stamps and selected IDs. Independent source review and exact bindings pass. Crucially, two ignored RR22 literal caller gates were separately executed and both FAIL freshly through that actual workflow: old preparation/model Value sites still corrupt marker objects. Those failures remain OPEN, not counted as provider passes. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR24/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate adoption/regressions and evidence. Snapshot 1c3dbf782ccfc3884f95c7c7ed9019b1e613135b preserves exact #82 606b169def89d2b4dabf6a48e03d16f3d024277b composition (#71\u2013#75 prerequisites) and six exact RR24a crate blobs from d16f6436ec5c133a7b5819c7e4198b57fe88f0e8. Initial red base9a29e467... is retained separately. Land #90/[RR24a #100](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/100) and composition prerequisites, retarget/requalify; never merge into this snapshot. No RR22/model ownership expansion. End-to-end literal, native/UI/product acceptance remains OPEN.\n\nAdmission metadata correction: the frozen batch packet's top-level snapshot_policy sentence retained the initial five-blob #90 wording. Its unit base, six qualified #100 blob identities and executed-source binding were already correct. Current plan admission explicitly corrects that sentence and records the superseded wording; original sealed packets and source heads remain unchanged.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 102,
