      "base_sha": "ca80c1960620f87b940bd1e2040597efd7842052",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T03:22:01Z",
      "body": "The observer opened a FIFO before its byte guard and could block. Admit actual regular UTF8 files of at most 1024 bytes using checked Linux x86_64 NONBLOCK/NOFOLLOW, pre/open/post identity/length/timestamp checks and a bounded read. Final symlinks refuse; stable ancestor aliases are supported. Other targets explicitly refuse. Existing suffix, grammar and observation output remain unchanged; no parser fallback or AST/semantic construction is added.\n\nVerification: immutable #12 FIFO CLI blocks until its reviewed owned child is killed and waited after three seconds, with no observation stdout. Six final tests pass: one exact self-child tests six deterministic replacement phases; five integration cases cover FIFO/type/symlink/UTF8/suffix refusals, exact1024/+1 with Unicode, ancestor aliases and byte-identical output for three original Rust #12 corpus observations. All six historical fixture/oracle bytes remain unchanged and compiler-bound. Scoped formatting, all-target Clippy, independent source review and exact committed-source bindings pass. Author SOURCE-FREEZE remains clearly pre-format preparation; executed hashes are separate. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR15/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate repair/regressions and evidence. Depends on #12 at ca80c1960620f87b940bd1e2040597efd7842052. Land prerequisites, retarget and requalify; never merge into the feature base. Stable parents are required; this is not openat/hostile-writer/device-race protection or a regular-disk deadline. Historical Rust output is not a fresh native epoch; full parity OPEN.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 101,
      "title": "Journal AST rollback and charge cancellable scalar copies (RR08)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/101",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr08-ast-rollback",
      "head_sha": "f0389bb7360bfa6246e66fe92144cb4b4eaa6269",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f12",
      "base_sha": "25acfaa6f3059685f133be034355f11104aad16f",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T03:21:56Z",
      "body": "Every transaction cloned the whole AST State, making growing construction quadratic. Replace snapshots with nested undo journaling for changed nodes/fields/arrays/kinds/frames/datatypes/CST. Charge selected scalar, kind and containment-label copies before reservation and poll cancellation in UTF8 chunks. Preserve rollback, owner identities, spent IDs/work and existing default limits. Copied bytes now consume work; root updates the inherited exact expectation from 3 to 17 without weakening its ID checks.\n\nVerification: immutable #41 construction at 100/1000/5000 nodes requests 3,312,488 / 333,251,536 / 8,350,409,616 bytes cumulatively; repaired identical fixtures request 34,844 / 335,960 / 1,673,112. Actual F12 stress is measured separately with an explicit fixture allowance; actual finite-parser construction is separately tested. First candidate passed 61 cases, then root found and freshly reproduced finish's uncharged repeated labels (2,106,112 bytes and wrong success); final guard refuses with 197,392 bytes. Both affected suites were requalified: 62 final cases (37 AST including nine new, 25 adapter), formatting and both Clippy gates pass. Independent review and exact committed inputs pass; original failures/passes and checked intermediate-source patches remain retained. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR08/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and evidence; 378 production additions/866 authored Rust additions fit the review gates. Depends on #41 at 25acfaa6f3059685f133be034355f11104aad16f. Land prerequisites, retarget/requalify; never merge into the feature base. Measurements are selected requested allocation traffic, not live/RSS/native speed or latency guarantees. Diagnostic-only unsupported strings/caller-owned clone APIs and panic rollback are outside this contract. Full native/application acceptance OPEN.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 100,
      "title": "Add explicit shared last-wins literal JSON compatibility (RR24a)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/100",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr24a-literal-duplicates",
      "head_sha": "9c95c9ef5fd297f97451e3884ba2eb618f3d2396",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr01-json-value",
      "base_sha": "ca7029b2a6c08393b172033e7bd9a548c2a66484",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T03:21:52Z",
      "body": "Native migration callers need final duplicate values at first decoded-key positions; the shared literal parser intentionally rejects duplicates by default. Add an explicit DuplicateKeys::LastWins entry through the same preflight, syntax validator, builder and materializer. Keep parse strict, preserve raw bytes/numeric lexemes/ordinary marker objects, and charge every physical occurrence before duplicate collapse. No second parser or key guessing.\n\nVerification: all 16 cases pass (11 original strict, five new policy), covering nested/escaped duplicates, overwritten invalid values, manual marker/token expectations, exact physical budgets and cancellation. The first root compile failed type inference for the key index; its receipt is retained and an explicit String/usize annotation fixed it before tests ran. Tests/fmt/Clippy pass on corrected code; later README-only discoverability update changed no tested Rust and required no test replay. Independent source review and committed-input bindings pass; intermediate states reconstruct from checked patches. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR24a/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate API/regressions and evidence. Depends on #90 at ca7029b2a6c08393b172033e7bd9a548c2a66484; this is a separate prerequisite for RR24 adoption. Land dependencies, retarget and requalify; never merge into the feature base. The old strict policy is not a bug. No new registry package or default-policy weakening; native/UI/product acceptance OPEN.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 99,
      "title": "Admit bounded regular snapshot files and pinned roots (RR13)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/99",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr13-snapshot-admission",
      "head_sha": "575345cdba6b0c1bc2d89f16cfacdd749b1535bb",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr13-base",
      "base_sha": "0c2cfb9764337f3d3b3730743c912e646be09c9e",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T02:34:47Z",
      "body": "Snapshot load could block opening a FIFO, and directory sync had another blocking open after publication. Require an absolute root without parent components or root/ancestor symlinks, retain a directory descriptor to pin identity, and check opened/post-read regular files with bounded size and matching metadata. Use checked Linux x86_64 NONBLOCK/NOFOLLOW for file and directory opens; other platforms explicitly refuse. Reuse RR04's bounded output before SnapshotIo staging while preserving its single write, no-replace hard link, sync/removal order and ambiguous post-effect failures.\n\nRead/output ceilings are 4 MiB, matching the inherited RR04 model admission cap; the prior 16 MiB outer guard could not admit larger models on this snapshot. Stable owned parents are required. This is not openat protection, a hostile-writer snapshot, arbitrary device-race safety, a regular-disk deadline or physical power-loss proof.\n\nVerification: immutable prerequisite FIFO load blocks until its owned child is killed and waited after three seconds. All 26 final cases pass: three new deterministic open races, eight new integration, two inherited connected and thirteen inherited fault cases. Exact children require one executed test and enforce kill/wait deadlines. Fixtures cover roots/symlinks/sockets/invalid UTF8, exact 4 MiB/+1, normal reopen/non-overwrite, pre-I/O output refusal and root-to-FIFO directory sync after publication with bytes/staging retained. Scoped nonrecursive formatting, all-target Clippy and independent source review pass; 167 executed inputs match committed blobs. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR13/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and evidence. Temporary base 0c2cfb9764337f3d3b3730743c912e646be09c9e preserves exact #32 762217dd56e6a0c4cd2aa2a01bfb62454bb8b6e9 plus ten unchanged #94 model/literal prerequisite blobs. Land #32/#94 and their prerequisites, retarget to integration and requalify; never merge into this snapshot base. No held factory feature or native/UI/full acceptance claim.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 98,
      "title": "Admit validator document bounds before parsing and cloning (RR21)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/98",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr21-validation-projection",
      "head_sha": "08b76c262e9669619af5feb4903823863d849b25",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr21-base",
      "base_sha": "3cc8784e00dc31715a30986ab97bcbfc68b57305",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T02:30:28Z",
      "body": "Selected semantic validation serialized/reparsed the entire Document and later cloned opaque data before shape refusal. Admit canonical size/depth through RR04 before parser construction, row collection or Snapshot cloning, then borrow the existing root authority. Set an explicit 1 MiB selected-validator cap, retain typed cancellation and preserve rule, source association, identity, warning and UTF16 behavior. Root registers only the existing pinned literal-value path dependency and locks.\n\nVerification: fresh immutable caller baseline requests 1,723,812 bytes below RR04's 4 MiB ceiling before refusal. Its raw live/peak statistics include an unmatched pre-existing Arc drop and are explicitly disqualified; largest-request evidence remains valid. Corrected final observers retain an outside owner: dense and ignored-envelope refusals request at most 64 bytes, peak 190 additional live bytes and retain zero observed bytes. All 25 cases pass: seven new and eighteen inherited, including #59 line-ending coverage, exact 1 MiB/+1, actual F14/F46 Unicode/CRLF warnings, deep provisional data, cancellation and late source errors. Initial reserved-name fixture failure is retained; only the fixture changed, then its executable and previously unexecuted rules/Clippy/fmt passed. Independent review and committed-input bindings pass. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR21/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and evidence. Temporary base 3cc8784e00dc31715a30986ab97bcbfc68b57305 preserves exact #59 f55c13f1bf96760ebd8c6d7906525273acd88fc8 plus ten unchanged #94 model/literal prerequisite blobs. Land #59/#94 and their prerequisites, retarget to integration and requalify; never merge into this snapshot base. Capacity tightening is explicit; requested layouts are not RSS, and full SysML/native/UI/product acceptance remains OPEN.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 97,
      "title": "Admit interchange JSON budgets before output allocation (RR05)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/97",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr05-interchange-budget",
      "head_sha": "c802bd768a3bcf87a026372de766ab447cfd21cb",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr04-json-writer",
      "base_sha": "26d3b2e82bc4b66de518872c4a620a84619e773b",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T02:30:24Z",
      "body": "Bundle and both identity bridges could allocate over their 1 MiB resource cap before refusing. Reuse RR04's canonical count/bounded owned output before cloning or emitting. Keep a shared compact transport with exact fallible reservation and a before-append bound; validated UUID substitutions are exactly 36 bytes in both directions. Preserve resource/node limits, identity domains, opaque values and private failure staging.\n\nVerification: immutable #94 produces two failing tests: Bundle and forward bridge request 1,048,687-byte outputs before refusal. The combined baseline bridge test stops before reverse; final execution reaches both, each refusing with a 40-byte largest request. Bundle's repaired largest 1,048,302-byte request is admitted scalar parsing, not refused pretty output. Original 500481-byte/16 MiB audit case is now an inherited RR02/RR04 refusal and is not reattributed to this repair. All 50 final cases pass (41 inherited, eight new integration, one transport guard), including actual F14, both bridges, exact 1 MiB/+1, accepted save/reload, numeric lexemes/private objects and wrong-domain refusals. Scoped formatting, all-target Clippy and independent source review pass; committed inputs match execution. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR05/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and evidence. Depends on #94 at 26d3b2e82bc4b66de518872c4a620a84619e773b and its prerequisites. Land prerequisites, retarget and requalify; never merge into the feature base. Requested allocations are not RSS/native capacity, and full native/UI/product acceptance remains OPEN.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 96,
      "title": "Refuse special and replaced composition input files (RR14)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/96",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr14-manifest-input",
      "head_sha": "e1c536a2455fb2ffdf4423b93362eff32a2e0b62",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c03a-composition",
      "base_sha": "9d244f04e76ae0ec3291416b733ae1e35b470905",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T01:53:06Z",
      "body": "The composition CLI could block indefinitely opening a FIFO manifest. Reject final symlinks, nonregular inputs and declared oversize before opening; on Linux x86_64 use checked NONBLOCK/NOFOLLOW flags and match opened/post-read regular-file identity and metadata. Keep the 2 MiB cap and existing Git blob/mode/global-delta checks. Ancestor symlink aliases are explicitly supported; other platforms refuse. Stable metadata checks are not a hostile-writer snapshot or regular-I/O deadline guarantee.\n\nVerification: immutable #77 FIFO counterexample blocks, then its bounded harness kills and waits for the child. Final 15 tests pass: three deterministic open-race cases, eight inherited and four integration cases. Race children have deadlines/kill/wait; fixed /dev/null is metadata-only refusal. Real owned Git CLI positives and blob/bytes/mode/delta negatives preserve manifest/index/config/refs. Scoped formatting, all-target Clippy, debug build and independent source review pass. A fresh actual CLI verifies the existing 93-selected-file plus one generated-file composition with 96 bound inputs unchanged. Historical 29 migration tests were not replayed or relabeled. Exact evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR14/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and evidence. Depends on #77 at 9d244f04e76ae0ec3291416b733ae1e35b470905. Land prerequisites, retarget and requalify; do not merge into the feature base. Bounded devtool repair only; application/native/UI/full acceptance OPEN.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 95,
      "title": "Admit storage fields before copies and SQLite payload fetch (RR12)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/95",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr12-storage-fields",
      "head_sha": "cf7d79603d435a3c77b8edf42f53a11df4bfaa33",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr11-db-generation",
      "base_sha": "e441af7de9f66146231295ef71519016d8c2141d",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T01:53:02Z",
      "body": "Oversized borrowed names were cloned and corrupt stored fields reached Python before refusal. Preflight all Rust mutation names at 4096 UTF8 bytes, then validate bounded row metadata/types/revisions and response size before payload SELECT in the existing RR11 snapshot. Set the actual connection's record limit, cap schema/generation projections and preserve CAS/rollback. Root's inherited RR11 test proxy forwards the real setlimit call.\n\nFresh candidates remain UTF8. External UTF16 v2 databases now refuse unchanged, including open_restored; no format rewrite. The Python bridge remains provisional pending B07. SQL C-engine allocations/RSS and native PostgreSQL are outside these bounds.\n\nVerification: baseline #89 reproduces a 2 MiB name copy and admits an oversized stored name. Final staged qualification covers 33 unique tests: two unit, eight RR11, eight new RR12 and 15 existing storage, plus scoped formatting/all-target Clippy and independent source review. Corrupt-field probes require zero payload SELECTs, metadata strings <=1024 bytes, bounded errors and unchanged DBs; max-valid rows and escaped responses pass. Whole-Python refusal peak allows 9 MiB including an existing 8 MiB stdin buffer. Original incorrect 256 KiB expectations failed at 8,390,218 bytes and are retained, alongside a root receipt-key failure before tests. Only the changed target and unexecuted remainder ran afterward; production/inherited bytes stayed identical. Exact bindings/evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR12/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and evidence. Depends on #89 at e441af7de9f66146231295ef71519016d8c2141d. Land prerequisites, retarget and requalify; never merge into the feature base. Local repair verification only; full Rust/native/UI/durability acceptance OPEN.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 94,
      "title": "Bound canonical JSON allocation and cancellable output (RR04)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/94",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr04-json-writer",
      "head_sha": "26d3b2e82bc4b66de518872c4a620a84619e773b",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr02-literal-adoption",
      "base_sha": "4e0b6dfd9688a64392a2ab91846761600c605a28",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T01:52:58Z",
      "body": "Document::to_json could allocate a 16 MiB buffer for a provisional dense document before refusing a 4 MiB publication limit. Promote the existing RR02 counter into shared json_size, to_json_bounded and write_json APIs; count/depth admission precedes owned reservation or external output. Keep the 4 MiB/depth-128 ceilings, exact canonical bytes and typed acknowledged-byte I/O errors. External failure or late cancellation can leave partial or complete output; callers own rollback, with no flush/durability or latency guarantee.\n\nVerification: baseline #91 reproduces 14,209,894 output bytes and a 16,777,216-byte allocation; repaired refusal has 40-byte largest request and 126-byte additional live peak. There are 100 unique qualified cases: 47 existing model, 12 new and 41 interchange. Initial 99 pass in rr04-01; test-only peer-requested final-write cancellation coverage passes with the 12-case target, scoped formatting and model Clippy in rr04-02. Other input bytes remain identical; both crates' initial all-target Clippy passes. Independent source review accepted final source. Held factory feature remains inactive. Original failures and exact committed-input bindings are retained at porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR04/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and evidence. Depends on #91 at 4e0b6dfd9688a64392a2ab91846761600c605a28. Land prerequisites, retarget to integration and requalify; do not merge into the feature base. Bounded local repair verification; RR05/downstream/native/UI/full acceptance remain OPEN.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 93,
      "title": "Roundtrip quoted parser keywords in text export (RR07)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/93",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr07-keyword-quote",
      "head_sha": "d705869afdc54104ff69bfee6a19f3982236c1c9",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr06-text-bounds",
      "base_sha": "0b1ac2d72f131322939227876ab561c5dbef073d",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T01:10:43Z",
      "body": "F14 could import package 'class', but export rendered class bare and failed its own importer gate. Quote declarations and qualified-reference segments using the existing NameHelper rule plus a small public query over the actual lexer keyword authority. Preserve standalone native NameHelper behavior and RR06 preallocation/shortest-reference rules; no duplicated production keyword list or lexer policy change.\n\nCorrected inventory: 170 lexer words and 117 NameHelper words overlap in 116, giving 54 lexer-only words and native-only constant, with 171 in the union. The old 53 was a net count difference. Seven new regressions cover all 54 extras in declaration/reference positions, the complete union, native helper controls, Unicode/case/punctuation, shortest/CRLF/indentation and exact 65536/+1 limits. Two old keyword-refusal expectations intentionally become successful quoted roundtrips; lossy/oversize refusals stay.\n\nVerification: baseline quoted-class counterexample fails on immutable #88; final affected parser/exporter suites pass 41 tests, formatting and all-target Clippy offline/locked. Actual F14 import/export/reimport and prior RR06 allocation tests run. Peer review corrected a self-shadowing fixture before execution and accepted final source. Exact executed inputs match committed blobs. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR07/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and qualification evidence. Targets #88 at 0b1ac2d72f131322939227876ab561c5dbef073d; land prerequisite, retarget to integration and requalify, never merge into the feature branch. This is an intentional export improvement with native helper compatibility kept separate; full text/native/UI acceptance remains OPEN. No merge/deploy.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 92,
      "title": "Prevent phantom nodes in physical library indexing (RR03)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/92",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr03-catalogue-literal",
      "head_sha": "38f6d6f3a5157f286e70ddc6fef7b1c53a37a490",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr03-base",
      "base_sha": "e234787259bb2a15c2ec5384b14f65b1a6e387de",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T01:10:40Z",
      "body": "Adopt RR01 in resource and manifest materialization so literal private keys cannot reify strings into physical nodes. Preserve exact raw carrier and separate resource-scoped node/semantic indexes. The original phantom payload now yields zero nodes through the actual repaired release CLI.\n\nAggregate actual-literal value/key and scalar-copy budgets are explicit. Depth now counts scalar leaves: the old container-256/scalar-257 edge refuses while value-depth 256 and the real depth-208 corpus pass. All existing file/node/index/walk/path guards remain. An additive cancellation API discards private staging without partial catalogue publication. These accounting/refusal differences are documented.\n\nVerification: 17 catalogue cases qualify across attributed stages; initial fixture-format compile failure and missing root-supplied CLI fixture environment remain retained. Only failed/unexecuted remainder was resumed on unchanged bytes. Formatting, all-target Clippy, release build and independent source review pass. Fresh CLI reads all 94 source-Git-matching files and matches all 109673 physical identity/class/name tuples against the retained hash-verified native capture. This is fresh Rust execution, not a new native epoch. The 12162 native diagnostics remain visible. One complete release process including 49MB output measured 0.39s wall/151104 KiB peak RSS; not p95/SLA/native speed ratio. Exact source/input hashes and failed attempts: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR03/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and evidence. Snapshot e234787259bb2a15c2ec5384b14f65b1a6e387de contains exact #85 plus five unchanged #90 crate blobs. Land both prerequisites, retarget to integration and requalify; never merge into this snapshot base. Physical indexing does not close semantic loading/reference/EMF/UI or full feature acceptance. No merge/deploy.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 91,
      "title": "Preserve literal JSON through model edits and identity bridges (RR02)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/91",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr02-literal-adoption",
      "head_sha": "4e0b6dfd9688a64392a2ab91846761600c605a28",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rr02-base",
      "base_sha": "58a1bbbd8244c7dd40acf0e8f5fa2041954109d9",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T01:10:36Z",
      "body": "Generic model Value parsing could reinterpret opaque private marker keys. Adopt RR01 once in Document::from_json; both identity bridges consume that authority transitively. Preserve literal objects, numeric lexemes and separate resource/node/semantic identities through actual Editor edit, both conversions and owned-file save/reload.\n\nThe selected model now explicitly caps raw/canonical JSON at 4 MiB and value depth 128, with typed duplicate/resource refusals. A private no-output canonical-size/depth counter guards imports and changed commits before history/revision publication, preventing accepted normal saves that cannot reopen. Bundle preserves its Limit error family. Staged/provisional clones are not claimed globally serialization-safe. RR04 must reuse/promote the counter; RR05 allocation work remains separate. These are bounded-admission changes, not native capacity or raw wire-order acceptance.\n\nVerification: two baseline model regressions fail on immutable #69 code; final default model/interchange suites pass 88 tests, including 13 new regressions, nonrecursive owned-file formatting and all-target Clippy. Independent source review accepted final source and restored scope. Original root dependency-wiring failure and recursive-formatter scope rejection are retained: five unrelated isolated-worktree files were restored to exact snapshot bytes, then both affected suites requalified; none is in the final diff. No raw-factory feature or canonical held source was changed. Exact executed inputs match committed blobs. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR02/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits: implementation/regressions, then qualification evidence. Base 58a1bbbd8244c7dd40acf0e8f5fa2041954109d9 contains exact #69 plus five unchanged #90 crate blobs. Land #90/#69 and their prerequisites, retarget to integration and requalify; never merge into this snapshot/feature base. Local repair verification only; full feature/native/UI acceptance OPEN. No merge/deploy.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 89,
      "title": "Refuse stale SQLite operations after database replacement (RR11)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/89",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr11-db-generation",
      "head_sha": "e441af7de9f66146231295ef71519016d8c2141d",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-audit-storage-budget",
      "base_sha": "6dc96e2cb4ef548656f4c9ac3a24f6e37ff9c194",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T00:30:52Z",
      "body": "Observations from database A could mutate replacement B with matching keys/revisions. Pin a persistent database generation and validate it on the actual opened connection inside the same read/IMMEDIATE transaction before every load or mutation, including create-only batches. Preserve row CAS, handle identity and batch rollback.\n\nThe local candidate format becomes v2; v1 refuses unchanged without implicit migration. Normal reopen retains the epoch. Explicit open_restored renews the epoch after caller-owned offline restore and invalidates prior handles. Callers must quiesce writers for file swaps; unannounced same-generation rewinds and swaps after a connection is open remain unsupported. The existing Python SQLite bridge remains a candidate pending B07 Rust replacement; this does not claim native PostgreSQL or complete Rust-distribution parity.\n\nVerification: both new stale update/delete regressions fail on immutable #64 baseline code, with original red results retained. Final source passes 25 Rust tests (two serializer unit, 15 existing integration and eight new generation tests), formatting and all-target Clippy offline/locked. Fixed owned-fixture wrappers exercise replacement between admission/connect, failed-renewal COMMIT rollback and WAL epoch/row snapshot interleaving. Independent source review accepted final source; exact executed inputs match committed blobs. Evidence: porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR11/RESULTS.md. RR12 bounds remain separate.\n\nTwo commits separate repair/regressions and qualification evidence. Depends on #64 at 6dc96e2cb4ef548656f4c9ac3a24f6e37ff9c194 (including #53). Land prerequisites, retarget to integration and requalify; do not merge into the prerequisite branch. Bounded local verification, feature acceptance OPEN. No merge/deploy.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 88,
      "title": "Bound text export allocations before output admission (RR06)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/88",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rr06-text-bounds",
      "head_sha": "0b1ac2d72f131322939227876ab561c5dbef073d",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f34",
      "base_sha": "82af0cea91e1a17c9b75e5bb77049357959ee50a",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T00:30:49Z",
      "body": "A 2 MiB model name previously returned the 64 KiB export-limit error only after a roughly 4 MiB allocation. Count the complete rendering before allocating output, retain borrowed names/qualified paths, and reject oversized names before copies. Preserve quoting, UTF-16 shortest-reference selection, LF/CRLF and indentation; RR07 keyword expansion remains separate.\n\nVerification: 13 existing tests pass on unchanged production/test bytes. The first new regression run retained seven passes and one invalid fixture using reserved `item`; corrected `wheel` fixture and all eight final regressions pass, followed by formatting and all-target Clippy offline/locked. Allocation observers bound the oversized-name refusal; exact 65535/65536-byte and CRLF/Unicode/indentation fixtures use actual F14 import/export/reimport. Independent source review accepted final source. Original failures and exact executed/committed hashes are retained in porting/rust-parity-evidence/RR06/RESULTS.md.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions and qualification evidence. Depends on #56 at 82af0cea91e1a17c9b75e5bb77049357959ee50a (including #52). Land prerequisites, retarget to integration and requalify; do not merge into the prerequisite branch. Locally verified bounded repair, NOT_ACCEPTED for full textual/native/UI parity. No merge/deploy.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 87,
      "title": "Read native project templates and bind observed choices (C01h)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/87",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c01h-project-templates",
      "head_sha": "a77137bb8c7dfa05acd08228e40aae57642d947e",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T23:16:21Z",
      "body": "# C01h: Read native template catalogues and bind template/control choices\n\nThe project-home flow needs the catalogue actually exposed by native SysON.\nRead ten fixed anonymous GraphQL observations, preserve the complete capture Value\nand raw bodies, and derive typed choices. Only the exact upload/browse IDs in the\nbrowser context are controls; blank projects, empty labels and ordinary IDs remain\ntemplates. Bind projected selections to a successful, unambiguous observed entry;\nvalidate selected nullable cursor presence without inventing pagination behavior.\n\nThe original eight tests pass. After independent review, two new isolated\nregressions, formatting, all-target Clippy and build pass on final source; no full\nten-test rerun is claimed. Eleven actual CLI cases verify five complete-capture\nroundtrips/correct selections and six refusals without stdout. All ten frozen\ninputs remain unchanged. The four native GraphQL errors and successful empty\nlater modal page retain their exact distinctions. Historical sources, exact\nqueries, native/CLI runners, receipts, streams and fixture are preserved.\n\nThis is observed discovery and choice preparation. C01/B23/U03, project creation,\npagination fixes, required-library resolution, provider/extension activation,\nsource/build correspondence and browser UX acceptance remain open. Native capture\nused a fresh owned derived reference; processes stopped and inputs stayed unchanged.\nNo production wiring or dependency acquisition is introduced. Final production/\nconservative authored counts are 300/853, within 400/900.\n\nTwo commits separate frozen source/query/fixture/preparation from execution\nevidence and disposition. Base `ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92`;\nno merge, deployment or service registration by this unit.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 86,
      "title": "Compare complete ordered JSON observations without normalization (C02a)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/86",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c02a-json-diff",
      "head_sha": "e91c25633859a17c17e6f170060f456ffc57d4c4",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T23:09:24Z",
      "body": "Actual native-versus-reader comparisons can retain different JSON member order even when map-based equality passes. This adds a reusable ordered JSON comparator that reports those differences, exact number lexemes, identities, types and null-versus-absence through separate left/right JSONPointers. It compares complete supplied documents without ignored fields, sorting, tolerances, profiles or internal subtree selection. Insignificant JSON whitespace and string/key escape spelling are the explicitly excluded representation axes.\n\nDuplicate decoded keys and malformed or over-limit inputs refuse. MATCH requires complete comparison with zero differences; a 64-difference reporting cap always remains incomplete MISMATCH. Both actual and hypothetical counterpart pointers must fit the bound. Read-only reports, bounded UTF8-safe source-character previews and compact output support diagnostic use. The CLI accepts two regular nonsymlink files and exits 0/1/2 for match/mismatch/refusal.\n\nVerification retains three distinct stages: c02a-01 passed the original nine tests, formatting, Clippy and build. Root source review identified the generated-pointer gap; the focused regression and whole-comparison refusal repair follow that capture. c02a-02 failed because the coordinator addressed the nonexistent test target `compare`; no test executed. Corrected c02a-03 passed the new focused test, formatting, Clippy and build. Ten regression functions are present; this does not imply a second full-suite run. Final independent source review passed.\n\nTwelve actual CLI cases passed the comparator contract: four native self-controls MATCH; four explicitly projected native-versus-reader observations MISMATCH; one genuine GraphQL identity mutation gives one precise difference; usage, duplicate-key and symlink inputs refuse. GraphQL and HTTP-probe reader comparisons reach the 64-difference cap and remain incomplete MISMATCH. The catalog pair covers capture metadata, not the whole database schema. Root prepared original UTF8 value-token byte slices with explicit projection provenance, without reserializing, sorting or normalizing them. The comparator performs no extraction itself.\n\nC01c #80, C01d #79 and C01f #83 supply the bounded observation prerequisites. Parent C01/C02, source/artifact authenticity, matched native/Rust functional equivalence and the broader harness remain OPEN. This unit runs no HTTP/SQL/native application and makes no performance or feature-parity acceptance claim. Base ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92; source and evidence remain in separate commits. Large prepared payloads stay external under exact identities; the genuine mapping fixture is committed once.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 85,
      "title": "Index actual native standard-library identities in Rust (C01g)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/85",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c01g-library-catalog",
      "head_sha": "df588dc53ca55e3d04464c06dc798e594fdd7d66",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T23:08:02Z",
      "body": "Add a bounded physical catalogue for shipped SysML/KerML library JSON, preserving raw bytes and exposing separate resource-scoped node-ID and semantic-ID lookups. The consuming CLI admits only bounded regular files under an explicit root and exports an identity index without fallback or a second semantic engine.\n\nValidation: nine integration tests, formatting, Clippy and both builds passed. The release CLI matched all 109,673 stored identity/class/name tuples across the actual 94-resource native corpus; exact runners, receipts, raw streams and external capture identities are retained. One process observed 0.34s wall/150,928 KiB RSS including a 49 MB index export, without an SLA claim.\n\nNative loading also recorded 12,162 package-not-found diagnostics. This qualifies physical catalogue behavior, not clean reference resolution, native fragment aliases, semantic loading, UI integration or full SysON parity. C01 and M15/M16 remain open.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 84,
      "title": "Plan and verify the selected native reference delta (C01e)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/84",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c01e-reference-delta",
      "head_sha": "dfab0235208ccd20a861b6860fbd79ea8f05e1cc",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T22:34:07Z",
      "body": "# C01e: Plan and verify the selected SysON reference delta\n\nBuild a reviewable comparison reference for the target source's known 125-path\ndelta. A source-aware Rust planner derives seven Java class-family replacements\nand 114 SVG operations across three nested modules; four documentation files stay\noutside the runtime overlay. It checks actual captured package/member ownership,\nold SVG bytes, class-family coverage, compiled identities, collisions, signatures,\nversioned shadows and complete bounded inventories. Admit only the pinned\nartifact's exact empty BOOT.SF marker and preserve it unchanged.\n\nNine original tests pass. After peer review, one new isolated SVG-shadow test,\nformatting, all-target Clippy and build pass on the final source. The final actual\nCLI recipe is byte-identical to the recipe already used by the native gates.\nSelected Java 21 compilation produces seven classes. Reassembly changes only three\nnested-JAR payloads, preserves 309 JARs and all unselected payload/declared metadata,\nand retains Spring Boot storage requirements. The derived reference passes 26\nselected provider cases, fresh owned startup, 114 exact target SVG responses and\ntwo GraphQL typename probes. Exact recipes, receipts, streams and original failures\nare retained; large inventories/artifacts stay external by identity, with the\nactual packet fixture committed once.\n\nThis is a selected-source-derived comparison artifact. Parent C01, an independent\nMaven/frontend build, full source/dependency correspondence, browser appearance,\nAPI/schema/DB/durability and application UX/performance acceptance remain open.\nNo native performance ratio or production-language fallback is introduced. The\nreviewed cohesive budget exception is 475/900 lines; final production/authored\ncounts are 469/820, including tests and manifest.\n\nTwo commits separate frozen implementation/fixture/preparation from exact execution\nevidence and disposition. Base `ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92`.\nNo application wiring, service registration, merge or deployment by this unit.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 83,
      "title": "Capture exact native HTTP mappings and observations (C01f)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/83",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c01f-http-contract",
      "head_sha": "9cb99468ca2d59eeae8965d66e52878611626216",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T22:20:41Z",
      "body": "The official native runtime returns the same 504-byte HTML frontend shell with status 200 for nine of the selected error/negotiation probes. Status-only comparisons would misclassify those responses. This adds an offline reader and CLI for actual Actuator handler mappings and 22 fixed anonymous HTTP observations, preserving every supplied mapping category/condition, repeated header pair, exact entity-body string/hex value and numeric value.\n\nThe captured application context contains 54 dispatcher rows, including 33 structured MVC mappings, five servlet filters and one servlet. The probe controls include an empty project list, absent-resource 404s, GraphQL JSON validation/syntax errors with status 200 and a denied CORS preflight with status 403. No HTTP behavior is implemented by this tool. A later Rust transport can make a reviewed usability improvement while recording its difference from the observed native shell responses.\n\nThe CLI accepts bounded regular nonsymlink files, emits the exact canonical probe manifest, checks complete condition families and fixed request safety, and streams compact JSON. `arbitrary_precision` preserves unknown large integers and native elapsed decimals without adding registry versions. Supplied artifact/source/configuration identities remain metadata; the reader qualifies their required shape and retains their values.\n\nVerification preserves the full sequence:\n\n- c01f-01: formatting and all 10 tests passed; Clippy failed on a production nested-if lint. c01f-02: the affected mapping test and formatting passed; Clippy then reached a test-only instance. c01f-03 passed the affected test, formatting, Clippy and build.\n- http-cli-01 retained a genuine probe Value-equality failure caused by four rounded elapsed decimals. The peer review also identified unknown-large-integer loss. c01f-04 passed all 11 tests, formatting and Clippy after enabling numeric preservation and adding raw-text integer/decimal regressions.\n- c01f-05 passed the final anonymous-context consistency test, formatting, Clippy and build. http-cli-02 passed seven actual CLI cases, including Python Value equality against both native payloads, exact manifest bytes and four no-output refusal cases. Final independent source review passed. These scoped stages do not imply a second full 11-test run.\n\nThe fresh native capture used only an additional loopback mappings listener with default access disabled and mappings read-only. Its receipt records the exact configuration and stopped owned processes. Native source label b380dada and target 6ba2ac64 remain distinct; parent C01 stays OPEN. Resolver/actions, authentication/session, multipart, streaming/WebSocket, business/model lifecycle, general API/Rust handler parity, default-deployment equivalence and performance acceptance remain open.\n\nBase: ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92. Exact root execution wrappers, raw receipts/streams/entity bodies, failed snapshots and numerical-fidelity correction are retained here. Native payloads are committed once as test fixtures; large original CLI stdout is referenced by exact external identity. Held paths and other crates remain unchanged.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 82,
      "title": "Preserve prepared-project wire payloads in Rust (C03c)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/82",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c03c-project-wire",
      "head_sha": "606b169def89d2b4dabf6a48e03d16f3d024277b",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c03b-project-preparation",
      "base_sha": "7f111c24bb3f79c44c55cdef2d4fa3246e50560b",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T22:18:45Z",
      "body": "# C03c: transport authoritative prepared-project wire data losslessly\n\nA prepared project's namespace order and independent migration stamps must survive transport. Add a local versioned codec whose encoder accepts only PreparedProject and reads its authoritative wire snapshot. Inline RawValue preserves payload token bytes without quoting/reformatting JSON; strict envelope metadata requires explicit nullable stamp keys and rejects duplicate, unknown or future-format fields. Decode returns untrusted ProjectInput for real C03b preparation.\n\nValidation: nine actual preparation/codec/replay and refusal tests, one compile-fail API test, formatting and Clippy pass. The lock retains the same 11 registry tuples. Candidate byte/item limits and no-quoting-amplification behavior are tested; no native archive/capacity, timing SLA, SQL or global acceptance claim is made. Exact receipts/streams, independent review and the supplemental inherited-fixture binding are retained.\n\nDepends on #81 at 7f111c24bb3f79c44c55cdef2d4fa3246e50560b. Land reviewed prerequisites, retarget and revalidate affected integration. Existing held paths remain untouched.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 81,
      "title": "Compose private project migration preparation in Rust (C03b)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/81",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c03b-project-preparation",
      "head_sha": "7f111c24bb3f79c44c55cdef2d4fa3246e50560b",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rp-four-migrations-base",
      "base_sha": "9baa77f9ce8c27cb0b784bee121872aab0ffcef5",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T21:28:21Z",
      "body": "# C03b: prepare a connected migrated project privately\n\nCallers previously had to chain semantic cleanup, document admission, library-ID migrations and diagram description-ID migration themselves. Add one typed project preparation API that calls the real B25b/a/c, Document, B01 and B25d paths in explicit order, retains separate stamps and namespace ordering, and returns matching wire/typed snapshots only after complete success. Late failures preserve input and prior output; external resolver effects remain caller-owned.\n\nValidation: ten integration tests, formatting, Clippy and release observer build pass. The prerequisite passes 36 composed tests. Fresh native-segment projects match whole JSON values and namespace eligibility, including foreign-first and intentional atomic refusal. Original Unicode capture failure and its explicit encoding repair remain separate.\n\nMeasured median preparation is 1.77/6.89/29.10 ms for 256/1024/4096 semantic nodes plus six diagram nodes, with ten measured samples after two warmups per size. Raw inputs/outputs/RSS/receipts/runners are retained. These synthetic measurements do not claim native capacity or UI responsiveness. Native B01 library/history/SQL and host/global acceptance remain open.\n\nBase: `codex/syson-rp-four-migrations-base` at 9baa77f9ce8c27cb0b784bee121872aab0ffcef5. Land reviewed prerequisites, retarget and revalidate; do not merge into the temporary snapshot. Existing held model/factory/initializer paths remain untouched.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 80,
      "title": "Capture and validate the effective native GraphQL contract (C01c)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/80",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c01c-graphql-contract",
      "head_sha": "604e6b6d929ea68d5f9f317724f5c49ff0fa4e4c",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T21:24:23Z",
      "body": "# C01c: read the actual effective GraphQL contract\n\nThe serde_json-only reader validates actual full introspection JSON and preserves the entire selected schema, ordered members, raw default literals, descriptions and deprecations. It checks types, field/input/argument wrapper chains, direct root/interface/possible-type references, enums, unions and directive definitions, and refuses missing selections, truncated wrappers, duplicate identities, incompatible/dangling references or GraphQL errors. The CLI reads bounded regular nonsymlink files and streams compact JSON; it makes no requests or source-regex/SDL guesses.\n\nFresh official-runtime capture `native-02` returned 671 types, 1,418 fields, 809 input fields and seven directives through five single-type capability requests plus full introspection. The original multi-type capability request in `native-01` was rejected by the unchanged native BadFaithIntrospection guard and remains an explicit refusal case. All owned processes were stopped with data isolated under owned artifact roots; the already-passed catalog capture belongs to C01d and was not replayed in native-02.\n\nActual debug logs list 46 loaded SDL resources. Exact artifact-resource byte provenance matches all 46 to four local SysON source documents and 42 inherited Sirius documents. The retained source inventory also lists forkstudio.graphqls, which was not loaded in this artifact/configuration; this is not a global absence claim. The effective schema is the actual response, not a count or inferred parse of those source documents. The artifact label remains b380dada while target source remains 6ba2ac64; 125 other paths differ and parent C01 stays open.\n\nVerification retains every stage: c01c-01 failed five helper cases after four passes because Query has no argument-bearing fields; c01c-02 passed all ten reader tests, formatting and Clippy after using actual Mutation arguments and enforcing named-only edge kinds. c01c-03 and c01c-04 passed scoped format/build/Clippy for later main-only guards/streaming changes, without replaying those ten tests or native capture. Actual CLI02 passed eight cases, including full native schema Value equality, the original native error refusal, invalid input/usage, exact query emission and one synthetic deep-opaque preservation case with compact output/input ratio about1.00064. That synthetic observation is not a general performance or native parity benchmark. Independent source review accepted the final core/tests/main.\n\nThe 681102-byte native response is committed once in the testfixture. [Actual CLI summary](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/blob/604e6b6d929ea68d5f9f317724f5c49ff0fa4e4c/porting/rust-parity-evidence/C01c/actual-cli-contract-summary.json) contains all observed counts/metadata and explicit full-schema Value equality; large original raw stdout/deep-synthetic files remain externally under exact [identity references](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/blob/604e6b6d929ea68d5f9f317724f5c49ff0fa4e4c/porting/rust-parity-evidence/C01c/c01c-cli-02/large-payload-identities.json). Raw request/header/status/response identities, executed wrappers, errors, captures and selected resource/source hashes are retained here. No derivative is labeled a raw stream.\n\nThis covers the observed standard introspection contract in the captured anonymous/configuration context. It does not qualify resolver/action/auth behavior, arbitrary applied directives, source/build/artifact equivalence, database/model/UI parity or other deployments. Base ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92; parent C01 remains OPEN. No held paths or plan lanes changed.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 79,
      "title": "Capture the native PostgreSQL contract for Rust comparison (C01d)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/79",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c01d-persistence-contract",
      "head_sha": "beac96785d12ce27712835726e4d74fd4c1968d5",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T21:20:10Z",
      "body": "# C01d: Project the native PostgreSQL catalog into Rust comparison obligations\n\nB05 needs the database contract actually created by native SysON. Add a read-only\nRust CLI that preserves native table, column, table-constraint, index and applied\nmigration descriptors as stable B05 obligations. Validate duplicate identities,\nparent/attribute references, complete foreign keys and target-owned backing indexes;\nkeep exact PostgreSQL type/default/expression text and migration order unchanged.\nInput/output and identity limits, incremental serialization accounting and\nregular-file guards bound projection without executing SQL or changing the input.\n\nFinal verification passes ten regressions, formatting and all-target Clippy\nunder offline/locked execution. Five actual CLI cases preserve every one of the\n164 native descriptors and the 20-row migration order, and refuse malformed,\nmissing-argument, directory and symlink inputs with no stdout. All nine frozen\ninputs remain unchanged. Independent peer review accepted the corrected source.\nThe supplementary 29 shipped DB XML resources match exact pinned Sirius Git bytes.\n\nRetain the original nine-case PASS, subsequent FK finding, CLI admission refusal\nbefore any launch, and shared native capture's overall partial status. Only its\nsuccessful catalog capture is credited here. Exact runners, raw streams, native\nfixture and selected resource inventory stay reviewable. The approved cohesive\nbudget exception is 520 production/1050 authored lines; final counts are 518/1042\nincluding SQL and manifest, excluding generated lock/data and prose.\n\nEvery obligation remains pending a Rust comparison. Parent C01, whole-build source\ncorrespondence and B05 behavior/schema acceptance stay open; sequences/views,\nfunctions/triggers/policies/privileges, type/extension and partition semantics,\napplication write isolation, DB driver/durability and UI/performance are separate.\nThe read-only capture transaction does not establish application write isolation.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/regressions/query/native fixture from exact\nexecution evidence and disposition. Base `ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92`;\nno application manifest/wiring, dependency acquisition, service change, push or\nmerge by the source author.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 78,
      "title": "Inspect current selected reference files and Git inputs (C01b)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/78",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c01b-reference-inspector",
      "head_sha": "a12d115f67d070fa21e9fca77a32195d5f5e9fa6",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c01a-reference-binding",
      "base_sha": "d592fe7332493b15e75b6538b5557f1fb262a3f7",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T20:23:37Z",
      "body": "# C01b: inspect current selected reference inputs\n\nThe read-only CLI consumes C01a's policy with actual root-contained files, Git objects and SHA256 observations. It checks the official application JAR, OCI config/manifest labels, four selected sources, nine dependency JARs, compiler/runtime/receipt/class hashes and the exact 125-path source-label delta. Effective classpath directories must contain exactly the nine JARs and five class files; extra classes, resources, files, directories and symlink entries/ancestors refuse. Internal file symlinks elsewhere may resolve to regular files inside the root.\n\nRoot capture `c01b-01` passed formatting and all 17 tests, then failed one test-only Clippy lint. `c01b-02` passed the affected symlink test (one test), formatting and all-target Clippy after the exact `from_ref` repair. The other 16 tests passed unchanged in the first capture. Both original captures and the original test source are retained; the second capture is not labeled a full 17-test rerun. Independent source review passed on final frozen hashes.\n\n`reference-runtime-01` ran the real CLI three times. The original historical request refused with exit 1 for the stale reviewed harness; the new scoped request returned exit 0 after inspecting 80 current files and exact classpath inventories, with `C01: OPEN` and `whole_artifact_equivalence: false`; missing usage arguments returned exit 2. The executed wrapper was retained before execution. Raw streams, source/program/primitive identities and both unchanged historical and new current review/request bytes are retained here.\n\nThe new scoped review records current retained input compatibility. It does not retroactively approve the old execution or prove historically unchanged dependencies. Inspection samples files individually rather than locking an atomic filesystem snapshot, and does not authenticate receipts/publishers, rebuild or bind the whole artifact, rerun the JVM/application, or qualify EMF/SQL/UI/performance parity. The official artifact label still differs from the target by 125 paths. The output retains actionable native-build/effective-configuration/inherited-capability requirements under open parent C01.\n\nCLI usage is `syson-reference-binding ROOT REPOSITORY REQUEST_JSON GIT SHA256SUM`. The exact tested invocations, root allocation and captured paths are in [the runtime receipt](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/blob/a12d115f67d070fa21e9fca77a32195d5f5e9fa6/porting/rust-parity-evidence/C01b/reference-runtime-01/receipt.json). Operator-selected primitives were `/usr/bin/git` and `/usr/bin/sha256sum`; no manifest chooses an executable, no shell or semantic fallback runs, and Git fetch/prompt/lock/hook/replace/external-diff paths are disabled. New real-file/inventory tests use only uniquely allocated data under explicit `REFERENCE_BINDING_TEST_ROOT`; they do not mutate live artifacts or constitute a separate positive actual-Git test. Actual Git/SHA consumption is established by the three CLI runs.\n\nBase: `codex/syson-rp-c01a-reference-binding` at `d592fe7332493b15e75b6538b5557f1fb262a3f7`. Land C01a through review, retarget/rebase this child, inspect the actual combined diff and revalidate integration. No parent-policy changes except the module export; no manifest/lock/README or held-path edits. [Metadata](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/blob/a12d115f67d070fa21e9fca77a32195d5f5e9fa6/porting/rust-parity-evidence/C01b/metadata.json) records exact scope and hashes.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 77,
      "title": "Verify explicit Git source compositions in Rust (C03a)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/77",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c03a-composition",
      "head_sha": "9d244f04e76ae0ec3291416b733ae1e35b470905",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rp-migrations-composed-base",
      "base_sha": "f19c06915a664eb636f6d0782c6d5191f9a43cd3",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T20:19:43Z",
      "body": "# C03a: Verify exact migration-source compositions in Rust\n\nOpen independent PRs need reproducible source assembly before integration. Add a\nread-only Rust CLI that checks local base/source/candidate refs and commit/blob\nidentities, every selected regular file and fixture, declared ownership and exact\nordered common-export generation. Missing/undeclared source changes, conflicts,\nstale heads, altered candidate bytes/modes, symlinks and escaped paths refuse.\n\nGit calls use structured arguments without hooks, filters, replacement objects or\nlazy fetching. Reads and selections are bounded. Source PR common files must be\nbase plus only their own declared exports; the candidate must be base plus all\nordered exports. The verifier never changes refs, index or user configuration.\n\nValidation: eight isolated real-Git regressions, formatting and all-target Clippy\npass offline/locked. The corrected actual CLI verifies93selectedfiles+1generated\ncommon file on immutable snapshot `f19c06915a664eb636f6d0782c6d5191f9a43cd3`.\nThe composed Rust migration library passes29distincttests with all97compiler\ninputs checked against committed blobs and no source drift. Earlier7-case PASS,\npeer owner-execute-bit finding and final8-case/runtime captures stay retained.\nThe final CLI runner was archived; the earlier inline runtime wrapper was not.\n\nThis qualifies selected source composition. Untouched inherited/untracked working\nfiles, remote PR freshness, whole C03 landing, application/UI/SQL/native parity\nand production acceptance remain separate. Parent C03 stays open. The coordinator\napproved482production/784authored Rust lines to keep the Git safety boundary in\none reviewable devtool.\n\nBase: `codex/syson-rp-migrations-composed-base`, exact\n`f19c06915a664eb636f6d0782c6d5191f9a43cd3`, containing source from #72\u2013#74 after\n#71. Land prerequisites through review, then retarget, inspect and revalidate.\nNever merge into the temporary composition branch. Two commits separate source\nand regressions from exact execution evidence. No push or merge by the author.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 76,
      "title": "Validate selected reference-binding evidence policy in Rust (C01a)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/76",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-c01a-reference-binding",
      "head_sha": "d592fe7332493b15e75b6538b5557f1fb262a3f7",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T20:10:09Z",
      "body": "This adds a pure policy core for selected-source-runtime reference claims. It checks the target revision, artifact/config/manifest relationships, four selected source bindings, nine declared dependencies, selected compiler/runtime arguments, compiled-class coverage and the source-label delta. Input observations are expressly `UnverifiedFacts`; success remains policy consistency with `file_inspection_performed: false`, `whole_artifact_equivalence: false` and `C01: OPEN`.\n\nRoot passed nine policy regressions, formatting and scoped Clippy on six unchanged inputs. Independent review found an actual retained-review contradiction: the historical review records an older oracle harness than the compiled sequence. The core now refuses it, keeps the original snapshot/example unchanged, and uses explicitly synthetic coherent facts for positive tests. This repair happened before the first root execution; no failed runtime is invented. Exact input hashes, raw root streams, peer disposition and the 125-path/native-build preflight are in `porting/rust-parity-evidence/C01a/`.\n\nOrdered child C01b adds actual contained filesystem/Git inspection and the read-only CLI, including bounded reads, path/symlink refusal and exact wildcard-JAR/recursive-class inventories. This PR does not inspect files/Git or authenticate receipts, bind the complete artifact/dependency source closure, rebuild/run the native application, or qualify deserialization/SQL/UI/performance parity. Parent C01 remains open.\n\nBase: `ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92`. Commits: `5fc6f0ed365b913712163fd990261e2563b6b26d` (core/tests/fixtures) and `d592fe7332493b15e75b6538b5557f1fb262a3f7` (evidence/preflight/limits). C01b must depend on this final verified head; land prerequisites through review, retarget/rebase children, inspect and revalidate actual integration. No held model/factory/initializer/backlog/plan-lane edits.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 75,
      "title": "Port action and control description-ID migration to Rust (B25d)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/75",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-b25d",
      "head_sha": "d8cc04372d184f5f51825cc7623047586a9ed7ab",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rp-b25-support",
      "base_sha": "cbf8a9f7a56f459a2374962e96010233fe711801",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T20:05:41Z",
      "body": "# B25d: migrate action and control description IDs\n\nStart/done actions and decision/fork/join/merge nodes can retain six outdated diagram description IDs. Add the exact 2026.7.0-202606240000 participant mappings, an explicit attribute callback, and bounded immutable preparation for Diagram content. Callback behavior uses the supplied current value. Local watermark selection stays separate from native framework history and B01 library-ID migration state.\n\nThe inherited native traversal visits nested objects and object elements of arrays. Nested arrays cause a native cast refusal; Rust deliberately publishes no partial output. Actual Java observations retain the native partial trees for both refusal cases.\n\nValidation: 16 tests (7 new + 9 shared), formatting and all-target Clippy pass. All 19 source-compiled Java/Rust callback and traversal cases match version, kind and status, plus JSON values/change flags on success. Exact runners, source/harnesses, dependency identities and raw outputs are retained with reproduction instructions. The actual B01 Representation handoff verifies independent watermarks and target-ID migration.\n\nThis qualifies selected callback/traversal behavior with candidate bounds. Whole artifact binding, framework activation, real editing contexts, native deserialization, SQL, GUI and durable publication remain open. Java exception text is retained without claiming Rust text equivalence.\n\nDepends on #71 (`codex/syson-rp-b25-support`, cbf8a9f7a56f459a2374962e96010233fe711801). Land prerequisites through review, retarget and revalidate affected integration. Existing held model/factory/initializer paths remain untouched.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 74,
      "title": "B25c: prepare ViewUsage exposedElement migration",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/74",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-b25c",
      "head_sha": "ac478624f5c78d247a624b887b5e8dd3666acbce",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rp-b25-support",
      "base_sha": "cbf8a9f7a56f459a2374962e96010233fe711801",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T19:21:28Z",
      "body": "Older resources can retain ViewUsage `exposedElement` values that became derived.\nPrepare participant `2025.6.0-202506110000` in Rust, removing only that exact\nserialized feature from the native helper's selected object-valued children.\nThe source comment's `exposeElement` misspelling, neighboring properties, node\nand semantic identities, and unrelated classes remain preserved.\n\nThe B25S prerequisite supplies bounded native-compatible traversal and namespace\nhandling. Callers use `Prepared::to_json()` between participants and resource\nadmission. This PR returns a complete owned result and selected participant\nversion; B06 still must publish project state and migration records atomically.\n\nValidation: 18 integration tests (9 new plus 9 shared), formatting and all-target\nClippy pass offline/locked; all 51 committed input hashes match `b25c-01`.\nThirteen identical-input cases match the selected Java source runtime for\nsuccess/refusal, version, resource predicate and JSON values. Tests also run\nactual Document admission and B01 preparation with stable identities and replay.\nThe shared parent retains four exact pinned Java classes compiled with annotation\nprocessing off against nine identified release dependency JARs; 728 predicate\nand four ordered-composition cases are common evidence.\n\nThis does not qualify the whole SysON artifact/source closure, complete model\ndeserialization, SQL publication or GUI workflow. Native exception text/classes\nand non-namespace object-key order are not asserted equal. Exact root inputs,\nstreams and this unit's native/Rust observations are retained separately from\nsource predictions and the original prepared packet.\n\nBase: `codex/syson-rp-b25-support`, exact\n`cbf8a9f7a56f459a2374962e96010233fe711801`, after B01/#70. Land prerequisites\nfirst, then retarget, inspect and revalidate; never merge into the support branch.\nTwo commits separate source/regressions from exact evidence.\n\n\nShared prerequisite: [B25S #71](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/71). The plan distinguishes bounded local/native observations from full feature acceptance. No merge is performed.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 73,
      "title": "B25b: prepare connector source and target migration",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/73",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-b25b",
      "head_sha": "23a48ab073cad592316bfa8d9b586e9d12d608de",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rp-b25-support",
      "base_sha": "cbf8a9f7a56f459a2374962e96010233fe711801",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T19:21:24Z",
      "body": "Legacy ConnectorAsUsage JSON can contain serialized `source` and `target` values that the pinned participant removes before deserialization. This adds the exact `2025.4.0-202502270000` participant over shared B25S: all eight connector-family classes, original first-namespace-entry eligibility, and removal from object-valued children of matching typed parents, including vendor children. Raw parent fields and unrelated classes remain intact. Callers compose output through `Prepared::to_json()` to retain namespace eligibility.\n\nRoot verification passed 17 integration tests (8 new, 9 shared), formatting and scoped all-target Clippy on 62 unchanged inputs. All twelve exact-byte cases match actual pinned-source Java and actual Rust observations for parsed JSON values, version, resource predicate and success/refusal status. Tests include participant \u2192 Document admission \u2192 B01 library-ID preparation with distinct watermarks and replay. The source-only peer review passed.\n\n`porting/rust-parity-evidence/B25b/` retains the unit runner, receipt, raw streams, actual Java/Rust outputs, input-only fixtures and separately labeled source predictions. The original unexecuted mixed packet is preserved. Shared B25S retains exact four compiled Java source pins, nine identified dependency JARs, 728 subtype predicates, four version-ordered compositions and earlier shared failures. Whole artifact/source closure, EMF deserialization, native global history, SQL/UI workflows and broad performance remain outside this evidence; Java exception text/class equality is not asserted.\n\nPrerequisite/base: `codex/syson-rp-b25-support` at `cbf8a9f7a56f459a2374962e96010233fe711801` (shared B25S PR pending at preparation time), above B01 #70. Land the support prerequisite through review; retarget/rebase this child, inspect the actual integration and revalidate. Do not merge this child into the support branch.\n\nCommits: `377d9d5cddddc05487013b79753c75ddd59eff7c` (implementation/tests/fixtures), `23a48ab073cad592316bfa8d9b586e9d12d608de` (evidence/disposition). All 62 captured source-input hashes and 32 unit evidence blobs were verified against the final committed bytes. Held model/factory/initializer/backlog paths are unchanged.\n\n\nShared prerequisite: [B25S #71](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/71). The plan distinguishes bounded local/native observations from full feature acceptance. No merge is performed.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 72,
      "title": "B25a: prepare Annotation reference migrations",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/72",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-b25a",
      "head_sha": "538f4c8a5ca6e4644ad020442a9e0056a91ac8bd",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rp-b25-support",
      "base_sha": "cbf8a9f7a56f459a2374962e96010233fe711801",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T19:21:21Z",
      "body": "Old SysON resources serialize `Annotation.annotatingElement` and its `AnnotatingElement.annotation` opposite, which became derived before 2025.4.0. Add the exact participant version 2025.4.0-202503140000 and ordered removals using B25S. Matching preserves the native first namespace entry and object-child/subtype traversal behavior. Preparation is immutable; callers use `Prepared.to_json()` to retain namespace ordering before replay or document admission.\n\nThe actual Document\u2192B01 regression admits the migrated resource and prepares it without resource loading, preserving identities and note text. Nineteen identical input cases match Java source-compiled native observations for output values, version, resource predicate and success/refusal. All 12 Rust tests (3 new + 9 shared), formatting and all-target Clippy pass at 49 unchanged input hashes. Exact unit runner/receipt/streams and19 native/Rust outputs are retained; source predictions remain labeled separately.\n\nB25S supplies the shared 728 subtype and 4 version-ordered composition comparisons, identified dependency JARs and bounded memory fix. This evidence qualifies selected participant preparation. Whole release source/artifact closure, global migration history, framework activation, native deserialization, durable publication, SQL and GUI remain open. Native exception text is retained without claiming equivalent Rust error text.\n\nDepends on `codex/syson-rp-b25-support` at cbf8a9f7a56f459a2374962e96010233fe711801. Land prerequisites through review, retarget this child and revalidate affected integration. No held factory/model/initializer paths change.\n\n\nShared prerequisite: [B25S #71](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/71). The plan distinguishes bounded local/native observations from full feature acceptance. No merge is performed.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 71,
      "title": "B25S: share bounded source-compatible JSON migration preparation",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/71",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-b25-support",
      "head_sha": "cbf8a9f7a56f459a2374962e96010233fe711801",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-rp-migration-pipeline",
      "base_sha": "e95d96ef3a49c0e504f4eccbf5201cbe1c5d8d3a",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T19:20:51Z",
      "body": "B25a\u2013B25c need the native MigrationParticipantService behavior: the first original namespace entry decides eligibility, and matching typed parents select their object-valued children. Add one shared bounded Rust implementation rather than repeating traversal.\n\nObject preorder IDs/postorder removal avoid cloned ancestor-key amplification. Prepared::to_json preserves current namespace values in original insertion order, including duplicate-key last values and removals; sorted Value serialization could change eligibility between participants. Input and edited output enforce 1 MiB,depth64 and65536-value bounds. Versions are selected metadata; no SQL or global migration history is persisted.\n\nValidation:9Rust regressions,formatting,all-targetClippy and releaseprobe build pass. Forty-four identical input cases match the actual three Java participants for values,version,resource predicate and success/refusal. Four version-ordered compositions and728subtype predicates also match. Java compiles four exact pinned source files against nine identified2026.9.3dependency JARs; this does not establish whole-artifact/source closure, native deserialization, DB or UI acceptance. Exception text/classes are retained rather than asserted equal.\n\nFor the identical143494-byte/128KiB-key/256-child release probe, actual process peak RSS drops36480\u21923264KiB (91.1%); compilation is excluded and both run under512MiB caps. This is one bounded workload,not a universal ratio. Original/intermediate/final captures and archival limitations are explicit in the evidence README.\n\nTwo commits separate implementation/contracts from exact evidence. Base codex/syson-rp-migration-pipeline (#70), exacte95d96ef3a49c0e504f4eccbf5201cbe1c5d8d3a. Plan#67 now registers B25S as an explicit prerequisite; B25a\u2013c target this branch only for focused review. Land prerequisites,retarget,inspect,revalidate; never merge into a feature/snapshot branch. No merge/deployment or held-path changes.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 70,
      "title": "B01: prepare versioned standard-library ID migrations in Rust",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/70",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-migration-pipeline",
      "head_sha": "e95d96ef3a49c0e504f4eccbf5201cbe1c5d8d3a",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-audit-storage-budget",
      "base_sha": "6dc96e2cb4ef548656f4c9ac3a24f6e37ff9c194",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T18:27:02Z",
      "body": "Prepare the two selected standard-library migration effects in Rust. Actual admitted semantic Documents migrate before recursive diagram targets; explicit no-load snapshot resolution preserves native library/nonlibrary precedence. Output and selected per-input watermarks return together only on whole-envelope success, with bounded escaped-JSON replacement growth and replay idempotence.\n\nNative SQL fixtures and mapping lines ground the two stable-ID expectations. This pure API performs no database or resource I/O and does not persist migration metadata or complete native F28. Atomic semantic/representation/watermark persistence remains B06 in plan #67.\n\nValidation:11integration tests,formatting and all-target Clippy pass offline/locked;40source input hashes unchanged. Tests cover actual Document admission, participant order, rollback, replay, nested references, nonlibrary precedence and aggregate expansion refusal before allocation. Exact runner,receipt and streams retained. No new registry version, native runtime, database or performance benchmark run.\n\nBase: `codex/syson-audit-storage-budget` (#64), exact `6dc96e2cb4ef548656f4c9ac3a24f6e37ff9c194`. Land prerequisites first, then retarget, inspect and revalidate; never merge into the prerequisite branch. Commits separate implementation/tests/provenance from validation evidence.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 69,
      "title": "I01: open native local identity wires in the selected editor",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/69",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-reverse-bridge",
      "head_sha": "f4e951a74c2a1b2d32db4d397ad4bddae3bbd173",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-audit-import-json",
      "base_sha": "d8fc0876714a0fcecb5548e9658ab0acf5cf1e53",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T18:24:10Z",
      "body": "Native JSON uses local node UUIDs for `FeatureTyping.type` and `typedFeature`; the selected editor and F14 importer use semantic element UUIDs. Add an explicit `native_model::load(..., LocalJsonNodeIds)` bridge for the same six package/part classes as PR #63. Both UUID domains, containment order and opaque JSON values survive. Conversion publishes a complete owned document after native reference and selected ownership-shape validation; wrong-domain, unsupported and dangling inputs refuse without mutation.\n\nThe integration journey opens native-form JSON, renames a usage through the actual Editor, imports a new package through F14, saves/reloads through F33, and reopens with unchanged identities and correct old/new typing. Same-class identity collisions ensure lookup uses only the declared node domain.\n\nValidation: coordinator `i01-03` passed all 36 integration tests (10 new and 26 inherited), formatting and scoped Clippy. Original `i01-01` mutation defect and `i01-02` lint failure, executed runners, main-crate sources and streams remain retained externally and hash-addressed by `verification.json`. Dependency inputs are hash-recorded and retained in the immutable base commit.\n\nThis is finite reference conversion. Native SysON runtime comparison, large-model performance, other classifiers, cross-resource references, resource loading and complete serialization remain pending C01/C02 and follow-on units. No production Java delegate, dependency or held factory/initializer change is introduced.\n\n\nBase: `codex/syson-audit-import-json` (#63), exact `d8fc0876714a0fcecb5548e9658ab0acf5cf1e53`. Land prerequisites first, then retarget, inspect and revalidate; never merge into the prerequisite feature branch. The two commits separate implementation/regressions from exact evidence. Full plan: #67.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 68,
      "title": "P01: preserve source positions while accepting lexical line comments",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/68",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-rp-line-comments",
      "head_sha": "c6c4696b009c5c5cfc61a4b206bcb64edf79c704",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f11",
      "base_sha": "ca1c4b3ab364db7dc9da835c66cba72912c3417f",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T18:23:12Z",
      "body": "Ordinary `//` comments now work in the finite package/part adapter through LF, CR, CRLF or EOF. Quoted slashes and escaped quotes remain name/reference content, original byte/UTF-16 spans are preserved, and comments consume source bytes without consuming visible tokens. Semantic `/* ... */` input and the overlapping `//*` multiline-note family remain explicit unsupported cases assigned to P05/P02.\n\nValidation: root ran 19 integration tests (13 inherited, 6 new), formatting and scoped Clippy on 32 unchanged source inputs. Ten fresh exact-byte fixtures were observed in the pinned native CLI and a separate real Rust adapter probe (46 inputs). Six selected class/name projections match; Rust positions and raw typing segments were checked against original source. Four differences remain explicit: semantic Comment support, hidden multiline notes, native recovered AST for a missing brace, and native ReferenceUsage nodes outside the finite Rust family. This is finite lexical evidence, not full AST/native-offset/application parity.\n\nThe original `p01-01` stale unsupported-fixture failure, the passing `p01-02` capture, all native/Rust raw streams, exact probe inputs and two wrong native-refusal predictions are retained in `porting/rust-parity/P01/`. Native CLI exit zero does not prove absence of parser recovery. Source-only independent review passed. No browser or performance acceptance is claimed.\n\nBase: `codex/syson-f11` (PR #40), exact `ca1c4b3ab364db7dc9da835c66cba72912c3417f`. Land or rebase after #40; verify inherited source closure before retargeting. Commits: `d069c0c33b4560e634c8adc9190ecfacd80ee601` (implementation/tests), `c6c4696b009c5c5cfc61a4b206bcb64edf79c704` (exact evidence/provenance). No historical F11 evidence changed.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 65,
      "title": "Keep diagram labels readable with actual-size and fit viewport modes",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/65",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-audit-canvas-viewport",
      "head_sha": "394b82a808f1650b63eeb2ef32516cc7ce99d4a8",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-base-audit-viewport-20261026",
      "base_sha": "0102549d7eb2d35833092a9b3eede55e967d20c9",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T17:13:03Z",
      "body": "The diagram preview scaled every model into the available column, making ordinary labels too small to read on a 320px screen. Add a readable Actual size view and an explicit Fit overview, keeping layout/history controls outside a labelled, focusable local scroll region.\n\nActual size renders admitted diagram units at 1:1, preserving 14px names and 12px class labels; large scenes pan using native keyboard or touch scrolling inside the viewport. Fit overview deliberately prioritizes seeing the whole diagram. The two 44px controls expose their pressed state, retain focus and change only page presentation: no WASM dispatch, model edit, geometry change or history entry. The selected view mode and earlier Actual-size pan survive ordinary repainting while Fit is active. This is ephemeral browser state, with no new pan/zoom solver or persisted representation semantics.\n\nThe new browser regression imports and lays out a real 32-node model at 320px and 1440px, measures SVG transforms and physical label dimensions, exercises native keyboard scrolling and Actual/Fit/Actual, and checks local overflow, focus, mode-only draft/caret/disclosure preservation and focused-caret restoration during background repaint and byte-identical model/geometry exports. Coordinator validation passes 44 inherited Rust tests, formatting, scoped Clippy and release WASM. The dedicated viewport journey passes with measured CTM 1, names 14px and classes 12px at both widths; screenshots were inspected. Five existing journeys collectively pass on identical production: inspector/layout in composed-02 and authoring/scalars/draft recovery in composed-03. Composed-02 remains FAIL overall; composed-03 ran only those three scripts. Original empty-export and blind-disclosure-toggle fixture failures remain retained and honestly dispositioned. Physical touch hardware, screen-reader speech and other browsers remain unqualified.\n\nThis follows recovery [#61](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/61) and navigation [#62](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/62) on exact snapshot `0102549d7eb2d35833092a9b3eede55e967d20c9`. Land those prerequisites, retarget this PR to the merged integration base, inspect and revalidate; never merge into the snapshot or prerequisite feature branches. Existing authoring, scalar, layout and inspector journeys must remain passing.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 64,
      "title": "Bound storage serialization before allocating oversized batches",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/64",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-audit-storage-budget",
      "head_sha": "6dc96e2cb4ef548656f4c9ac3a24f6e37ff9c194",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f27",
      "base_sha": "b540273b901f9c69b5fc2f200efc1aa864d95ebc",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T16:41:27Z",
      "body": "A valid 64-operation batch could exceed the 8 MiB protocol limit only after every near-limit document and the full JSON packet had been allocated. Stream each serialized operation into one bounded request, cap writer capacity, and invoke the unchanged fixed SQLite bridge only after the complete packet fits. Per-document writer failures remain Serialization; aggregate exhaustion remains Limit and stops before SQL.\n\nThe identical release API probe reuses one 1,048,448-byte document in 64 distinct-key creates. Both runs refuse the aggregate and preserve initialized database bytes. Actual-command maximum RSS falls from 267,536 KiB (261.3 MiB) to 13,332 KiB (13.0 MiB), about 95.0% lower; Rust compilation is excluded. This is one fixed before/after workload, not a native PostgreSQL or universal latency claim.\n\nAll 17 tests (2 budget tests and 15 integration cases), formatting, scoped all-target Clippy and release build pass offline/locked. New cases cover escaped JSON/final delimiters, allocation capacity, large aggregate refusal and successful escaped 64-operation packets; original serializer and late SQL rollback cases remain passing. Exact executed runner/input snapshots/raw streams, probe/binary hashes and external SQLite hashes are retained. Python bridge, schema, tool fingerprints, manifests and dependencies are unchanged. Coordinator independent source review found no blocking issue.\n\nCode/tests/probe and generated evidence/docs are separate commits. Depends on F27 #53; land it first, retarget to integration and inspect/revalidate, never merge into its feature branch. Native persistence, authorization and crash durability remain outside this local candidate.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 63,
      "title": "Bridge selected import identities to native JSON references explicitly",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/63",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-audit-import-json",
      "head_sha": "d8fc0876714a0fcecb5548e9658ab0acf5cf1e53",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-base-audit-import-json-20261026",
      "base_sha": "4f4ad801796081cf337fac81c29e0e5617f3cc9a",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T16:41:23Z",
      "body": "Text import uses semantic element IDs for selected-model typing, while native JSON references use node UUIDs. Passing a selected document directly to native loading can either fail or silently select another same-class object when the two identity domains collide. Add an explicit caller-selected bridge for the finite F14 package/part family; native Bundle::load keeps its existing contract.\n\n`selected_model::load` requires a LocalSemanticElementIds source tag, validates each FeatureTyping against its containing usage and local PartDefinition target, then rewrites only type/typedFeature on an owned clone before normal native bundle admission. Node IDs, semantic IDs, envelope and opaque unknown values remain intact. Missing/external/malformed references, unsupported shapes and late failures publish nothing; no identity fallback or resource loading is attempted.\n\nRegression coverage uses the actual F14 importer, native save/reload, nested FeatureMembership/cross-package typing and a complete cross-domain collision permutation that proves the exact intended type and usage survive conversion. The final coordinator capture passes all 26 integration tests (14 inherited plus 12 bridge tests), formatting and scoped all-target Clippy offline/locked. All 114 captured input hashes match committed bytes; exact original source, runners, receipts and streams for both passing captures are retained. Independent coordinator source review found no blocker within this finite scope. This is a finite one-way reference representation bridge, not complete native serialization or reverse native-to-selected textual export.\n\nDepends on F33 #55 and F14 #52, targeting their exact frozen prerequisite snapshot. Land the prerequisites, retarget to the merged integration base, inspect and revalidate; never merge into the snapshot. The F14 dependency is test-only; no new registry package or held model/initializer/factory path is changed.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 62,
      "title": "Clarify model hierarchy and preserve staged-edit selection context",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/62",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-audit-ui-navigation",
      "head_sha": "d11ab28e077351a5b1c28673b03937d20a179ed9",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f36",
      "base_sha": "d8f30b9c05df2f6ccb6311c308bac06f55e0b3cc",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T16:41:20Z",
      "body": "The model explorer mixed unnamed relationship objects with packages/parts, and secondary property forms crowded ordinary editing. Nest semantic elements by actual owner, keep every relationship selectable in a labeled disclosure, and group uncommon properties while leaving common editing controls visible. Preserve advanced-property focus through staging, and refuse selecting B while an edit on A is pending so commit and inspector context stay aligned.\n\nThe existing styling gains 44px control targets, bounded indentation, wrapped actions and 320px reflow. No model capability, property editor, identity/history behavior or loader source is removed or replaced. Final validation passes 44 native tests, formatting, scoped Clippy and release WASM. Four actual browser journeys pass on nav-02; the changed keyboard/AX inspector journey passes again on final nav-03, covering wrong-B selection, advanced disclosure focus, live-region continuity and desktop/390px/320px sizes. Independent source review found no blockers.\n\nOriginal captures remain intact. Receipts/runners/streams and explicit later-recovery metadata preserve the old browser input honestly; binaries/screenshots/full AX trees remain external. Canvas zoom/fit, small mobile diagram labels, cross-browser/touch-device studies and screen-reader speech remain unqualified. Depends on F36 #51: land it first, retarget and revalidate; never merge into its feature branch. Composition with the separate loader draft-preservation fix is coordinator work, not claimed by this standalone branch.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 61,
      "title": "Preserve unsaved drafts through canvas history and failed actions",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/61",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-audit-ui-recovery",
      "head_sha": "5e9221fafa02c90490a21b343f6e22271e0eac27",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f36",
      "base_sha": "d8f30b9c05df2f6ccb6311c308bac06f55e0b3cc",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T16:41:16Z",
      "body": "Canvas undo/redo/cancel now preserve unrelated form drafts and disclosure state. Rejected operations retain entered values for correction, and focus targets open their disclosure ancestors so recovery remains reachable. Successful model edits keep their existing reset behavior.\n\nThe audit reproduced canvas undo replacing an unsaved rename with its committed value. A committed actual-browser regression now covers canvas history/cancellation, rejected creation, independent draft retention, disclosure state and unchanged model bytes. Native checks pass 41 tests, formatting, Clippy and release WASM; fresh desktop/mobile walkthroughs and the final focused browser capture pass. An independent source review found no blockers. Error-path caret retention is outside this claim.\n\nDepends on F36 #51. Land the prerequisite, retarget to integration, inspect and revalidate; never merge into the feature branch. Code/browser regression and audit disposition are separate commits. Nothing is merged or deployed.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 60,
      "title": "Index document reconciliation while preserving identity and order",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/60",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-audit-reconcile-index",
      "head_sha": "a85366ae8252596b417384d02e0ded6784d93eed",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f25",
      "base_sha": "b454d4991d2518dd58ecab29ddcffe012823c46d",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T16:41:12Z",
      "body": "An unchanged document update repeatedly scanned pointer identities, existing UUIDs and prior outputs. Replace those scans with standard-library identity sets and a first-existing-UUID index while preserving caller order, duplicate-UUID first-match behavior, object identity and ordered timestamp/event requests.\n\nThe same frozen release benchmark improves the 10,000-document unchanged workload from 55.109 ms to 0.897 ms median (61.46\u00d7 over five samples); 1k/5k medians also improve. A 2,048-document mixed regression covers repeated pointers, pointer-distinct equal UUIDs, first-existing selection, reverse incoming order, separate rebuilds and exact effect positions. All 16 tests, formatting and scoped all-target Clippy pass offline/locked. Exact runners, source snapshots and raw before/after outputs are retained, including the original passing-tests/failed-test-style capture.\n\nNo manifest/dependency change or database/UI/native Java runtime is introduced. Timings qualify this Rust workload and host, not universal tiny-input performance or native SysON speed. Cargo-build RSS is not claimed as planner-only memory. Depends on F25 #24; land that prerequisite first, retarget to integration, inspect and revalidate rather than merging into its feature branch. Code/regression/benchmark and generated evidence/documentation are separate commits. Independent coordinator source review found no blocking issue within this scope.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 59,
      "title": "Correct diagnostic positions across CR, LF and CRLF",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/59",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-audit-source-lines",
      "head_sha": "f55c13f1bf96760ebd8c6d7906525273acd88fc8",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f47",
      "base_sha": "37d1800cb9858f5d62ac244963dad031ffe3b410",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T16:38:44Z",
      "body": "Source diagnostics for CR-separated models pointed to line 1 or retained the wrong column after mixed line endings. Count CRLF as one break and bare CR/LF as one each, while measuring columns in UTF-16 code units and preserving the original byte/UTF-16 declaration spans.\n\nThis follows the finite F11 lexer, which already accepts CR and LF as whitespace. Regressions exercise all 27 CR/LF/CRLF separator combinations with Unicode names and mixed leading breaks with supplementary characters. The coordinator first reproduced both failures against unchanged production source; exact original inputs, runner, receipt and streams are retained. The green capture passes all 18 integration tests, formatting and scoped all-target Clippy offline/locked; all captured inputs are unchanged. Coordinator and independent source review found no blocking issue within this finite source-position scope.\n\nDepends on F47 #57. Land that prerequisite first, retarget to the merged integration base, inspect the diff and revalidate; never merge into the prerequisite feature branch. This fixes the finite validator's source-position usability; native AQL/application source-map parity remains unverified.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 58,
      "title": "Fix linker admission at the 256-declaration parser boundary",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/58",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-audit-linker-limit",
      "head_sha": "6fe12e6bd256f9fcb2284b60b8d6d97ab53100fc",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f13",
      "base_sha": "aac4d2fd46d6f1c96358fa67bc017a4bcba85c5c",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T16:31:59Z",
      "body": "The linker counted F11's anonymous Namespace as a real declaration, so a valid 256-declaration text model failed with `Limit` after parsing successfully. Count only real declarations against the 256 limit; a custom Package root still counts as a real declaration.\n\nThe regression exercises the actual default F11 parser at 255/256 declarations and resolves a reference to the final definition. Separate tests retain the 257-declaration refusal with both default and expanded parser budgets, and verify that a real Package root receives no synthetic-root allowance.\n\nThe coordinator preserved the original failing `link-red-01` capture (17 passed, one failed with `Limit` at 256 real declarations), including exact executed source, runner and raw streams. After the repair, `link-green-01` passes all 19 integration tests, formatting and scoped all-target Clippy offline/locked, with all 68 captured input hashes unchanged. Independent coordinator source review found no blocker. Exact source, runner, receipts and streams for both attempts are retained; the PR includes a compact validation summary. No native language limit or full parser parity is claimed; this aligns the two existing finite Rust admission budgets.\n\nDepends on F13 #50. Land the prerequisite first, retarget to the merged integration base, inspect and revalidate; never merge into the prerequisite branch. The change is limited to linker admission and four boundary regressions, with no new dependency or held model/initializer/factory path changes.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 57,
      "title": "F47: Validate selected namespace names and direct part typing with source spans",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/57",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f47",
      "head_sha": "37d1800cb9858f5d62ac244963dad031ffe3b410",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-base-f47-20261026",
      "base_sha": "259ecebe50ed80debf7a8bf0506c7bb3a600a214",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T15:10:22Z",
      "body": "Package/part validation needs explicit coverage and source locations. Add a finite immutable validator for the current upstream namespace distinguishibility and PartUsage PartDefinition rules. It checks the source/model declaration association, uses actual F11 spans and F46 owner/name operations, and reports warning diagnostics with byte/UTF-16 positions. Tests compose actual F14 import with valid and edited selected documents.\n\nOnly the six frozen classifiers and two explicitly requested rules are admitted. Unknown rules/classes, unsupported containment, source mismatch and unresolved typing refuse. Local typing preserves F14 semantic-ID encoding without node-ID fallback; no full SysML/AQL/native EMF qualification is claimed. Exact prerequisite snapshot: F14 #52 plus F46 #49. Land both first, retarget and revalidate; never merge into the snapshot.\n\nValidation: coordinator serial offline/locked checks pass all 16 integration tests, formatting and scoped all-target Clippy. Ten exact source pins pass. Original receipt, six output streams, exact executed runner and input snapshots are retained; all captured input hashes are unchanged. The inherited initializer fetch_update deprecation warning remains in the original output. Coordinator and independent F34 source reviews found no blocking issue within the selected scope. Native upstream AQL/application runtime remains unrun.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 56,
      "title": "F34: Export finite package and part text with round-trip admission",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/56",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f34",
      "head_sha": "82af0cea91e1a17c9b75e5bb77049357959ee50a",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f14",
      "base_sha": "574193c29659010bd5c31c1e6a768fb58f712230",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T15:10:19Z",
      "body": "Selected package/part models can now export a complete deterministic UTF-8 textual form, including ordered containment, explicit indentation/newline options and local semantic-ID typing. The finite containment resolver chooses a shortest name only if it resolves to the original target; dangling, shadowed, unsupported or potentially lossy inputs return an error without publishing partial output.\n\nEvery successful export passes through actual F14 private staging and an identity-independent declaration/typing comparison before bytes are returned. The finite whitelist excludes native EMF wire forms, imports/aliases/modifiers and wider exporter families; no native SysON/Syside runtime equivalence is claimed. Apostrophe/backslash/control names and the wider F11 reserved-name boundary have explicit refusal cases.\n\nDepends on F14 #52. Land that prerequisite first, retarget this PR to the merged integration base, inspect the diff and rerun appropriate checks; never merge into the prerequisite feature branch. Nine source pins and 13 coordinator integration tests pass, with formatting and scoped all-target Clippy offline/locked. All 76 captured source inputs are unchanged; exact runner, receipt and six raw streams are retained. Independent source review found no blocking issue within this finite scope.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 55,
      "title": "F33: Round-trip finite cross-resource EMF JSON reference bundles",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/55",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f33",
      "head_sha": "92aaccaf5cd5b69b44839f77dff7723e078a60fa",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f05",
      "base_sha": "80261b68e5e7ec2f2fe7f0d638050faca9800670",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T15:10:14Z",
      "body": "Selected JSON uploads need to retain resource/node/semantic identities across save and reload. This finite immutable bundle adapter privately parses every caller-supplied resource, resolves FeatureTyping type/typedFeature with F04, and returns a complete bundle only after all checks pass. It retains opaque unknown JSON values and preserves wire strings; serialization emits pretty JSON without claiming upload-byte preservation.\n\nThe scope is exact package/part/port/view classes, owning/feature memberships and FeatureTyping. Known metamodel reference features outside the admitted pair refuse. Missing/dangling libraries, unsupported encodings, wrong target classes, duplicate identities and late malformed resources never publish partial staging. No resource discovery/loading, native serializer defaults/caches, complete Batmobile admission or full SysML validity is claimed. An actual F05 GeneralView construction is exercised through save/reload.\n\nF33 targets F05 #54, which includes F04 #47. Land prerequisites, retarget to integration and inspect/revalidate; never merge into a prerequisite branch. The worker source-pin checker passes six immutable source hashes and verifies actual native fixture local-node/external-library identity examples. Coordinator validation passes 14 integration tests, formatting and scoped all-target Clippy offline/locked. Exact executed runner, six raw streams and unchanged input hashes are retained. Canonical saved-byte admission was repaired during source review before the first capture; no failed compiler/test capture occurred. Independent coordinator source review found no blocking issue within the declared finite scope.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 54,
      "title": "F05: Stage selected ViewUsage construction with scoped GeneralView references",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/54",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f05",
      "head_sha": "80261b68e5e7ec2f2fe7f0d638050faca9800670",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-base-f05-20261025",
      "base_sha": "46a79b3a265965768220f2976b79a842b05649c1",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T00:08:31Z",
      "body": "ViewUsage initialization needs one atomic construction and a scoped GeneralView target. This standalone adapter runs the existing F01 plan over an actual attached prefix projection, then appends one finished membership/ViewUsage/FeatureTyping subtree to the caller's owned transaction. Caller NodeIds retain separate node and semantic identities; commit remains explicit and existing model history/revision checks stay authoritative.\n\nThe internal query provider materializes name/composite/allocation/attachment effects at the real query point. Local type/typedFeature references use JSON node identity; external GeneralView references retain typed library URI and semantic-fragment scope and are checked through F04. Known absence assigns null, reached unresolved input refuses, and cancellation/collision/late encoding failure publishes nothing. No caller plan or foreign target handle is accepted.\n\nThis finite selected-JSON construction uses public default-feature admission. It leaves held graph/factory paths unchanged and does not qualify native factory defaults, caches, import evaluation, full EMF serialization or graphical creation. Seven exact source pins and the actual Batmobile ViewUsage wire shape pass. Coordinator validation passes 12 integration tests, formatting and scoped all-target Clippy. The exact original runner, all 69 captured input hashes and six raw streams are retained. The inherited initializer deprecation warning remains in the original output; its source is unchanged. Independent parent source review found no blocking issue within this selected family.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 53,
      "title": "F27: Add transactional local selected-document storage with SQLite",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/53",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f27",
      "head_sha": "b540273b901f9c69b5fc2f200efc1aa864d95ebc",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-base-f27-20261025",
      "base_sha": "466517a8f4ba51dec0fa30706a292baeee9eb822",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T00:08:12Z",
      "body": "Selected model JSON had no transactional reloadable store. This isolated SQLite candidate adds create/update/delete/reload over explicit project/document UUID keys, preserving the model's separate JSON-node and semantic IDs. Batches use fixed parameterized SQL, one transaction, stored read-only/revision checks and monotonic revisions across delete/recreate. Actual F25 reconciliation controls update/no-op decisions; actual F04 reference lookup verifies reloaded identity behavior. Serializer errors occur before SQL; late SQL failures roll back the whole batch.\n\nThe bridge uses the installed Python standard-library SQLite through a fixed isolated subprocess, with no new registry package, service or network target. Fresh-file ownership and exact candidate-format checks prevent implicit creation on reads and refuse mismatched existing files before writes. Tool versions, hashes, exact subprocess/SQLite boundaries and owned workspace test paths were reviewed by the coordinator before execution.\n\nValidation: 13 integration tests, formatting, scoped all-target Clippy and eleven source pins pass. Tests cover reopen, cross-project equal IDs, read-only/stale/foreign observations, real serializer writer failure, late SQL rollback, delete/recreate and format drift. Original runner, raw streams, unchanged-source/tool fingerprints and DB-artifact hashes are retained; synthetic DB files remain outside Git. No failed compiler/test attempts occurred.\n\nThis is a bounded local selected-document adapter. The F26 native schema/artifact blockers remain unresolved; no PostgreSQL migrations, native SysON/EMF runtime, production target, security policy, timestamp/event publication or crash/power-loss durability qualification ran. The PR depends on the frozen F04/F25/F26 snapshot; land those prerequisites before retargeting and revalidating, and never merge into the snapshot branch.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 52,
      "title": "F14: Stage finite package and part text imports atomically",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/52",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f14",
      "head_sha": "574193c29659010bd5c31c1e6a768fb58f712230",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f13",
      "base_sha": "aac4d2fd46d6f1c96358fa67bc017a4bcba85c5c",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-26T00:07:12Z",
      "body": "Package/part text had separate finite AST and linker adapters but no atomic path into the selected model. This importer composes those real prerequisites with one owned model transaction: create all declarations, resolve forward/qualified local references through explicit AST-to-JSON-node bindings, then stage typing for a single caller commit. Cancelled, malformed, unresolved, stale, foreign or colliding work cannot publish a partial import.\n\nThe finite family is named packages, part definitions and usages. Explicit caller NodeIds preserve semantic/resource identity. Existing model typing retains its semantic-ID string encoding; native bare-reference interchange remains excluded. Current Java declaredName apostrophe stripping is pinned through the actual importer/attribute call chain, including its escaped-name quirk; AST lookup remains independent of transformed labels.\n\nValidation: thirteen Rust integration tests, formatting, all-target Clippy and eight source pins pass. Tests exercise actual parser/linker/model composition, forward references, selected containment, identity distinctions, quote translation, cancellation and failure/history boundaries. The original 10-pass/three-failed fixture capture and corrected passing capture retain exact executed sources, runners, streams and unchanged-input hashes. Independent parent source review found no blocking issue within the finite scope. No native Syside/Java importer or complete SysML interchange is claimed. This PR follows F13, which contains the exact F11 prerequisite; land prerequisites, retarget and revalidate. Held graph/factory paths and shared manifests remain unchanged.\n\n\nDepends on [F13 #50](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/50), which contains the exact [F11 #40](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/40) prerequisite. Land prerequisites first, then retarget and revalidate; do not merge into the prerequisite feature branch.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 51,
      "title": "F36: Preserve inspector focus and live-region accessibility across edits",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/51",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f36",
      "head_sha": "d8f30b9c05df2f6ccb6311c308bac06f55e0b3cc",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f19",
      "base_sha": "797b1c194b1cd46f0152b257d337e6cf2983041c",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T23:21:54Z",
      "body": "Inspector actions repainted the whole editor, dropping focus from unnamed controls and recreating the status live region. This change gives selection/staging/completion a small Rust-owned focus policy, stable control IDs and named inspector/forms. Commit/cancel return to the originating field. The loader preserves the existing status node continuously while repainting its siblings, applies only changed attributes/text and retains background canvas draft/caret behavior.\n\nValidation: 41 Rust tests (one new actual App staging/focus regression plus 40 inherited), formatting, all-target Clippy, release WASM and four actual browser journeys pass. The new keyboard journey creates a package/definition/typed usage and checks selection, rename/boolean stage/cancel/commit, tab order and origin focus. Full Chromium CDP accessibility trees verify labels, focus and live/atomic semantics with one persistent backend status node; DOM observation confirms continuous connection. Desktop/mobile console errors/warnings are empty for the new journey, and the coordinator inspected focus/label screenshots. Exact original runners/streams/hashes and small focus/live/AX summaries are retained; screenshots/full AX trees stay outside the repository. The earlier passing native-only capture is preserved before a test-observer refinement.\n\nThe five source pins identify the inherited application/custom-label source and exact local F19C baseline. Browser accessibility semantics do not establish screen-reader speech or native SysON parity; those remain unrun, along with other browsers/platforms and whole-app acceptance. This PR follows F19C and changes no model semantics, manifests, held graph path, dependency or production service.\n\nIndependent source-only review found no blocking issue within the documented focus/live-region scope. The existing canvas draft/caret journey also passes against the resulting WASM.\n\n\nDepends on [F19C #45](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/45). Land the prerequisite, then retarget and revalidate this child; do not merge into the prerequisite feature branch.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 50,
      "title": "F13: Link finite local AST references with explicit semantic bindings",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/50",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f13",
      "head_sha": "aac4d2fd46d6f1c96358fa67bc017a4bcba85c5c",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-base-f13-20261025",
      "base_sha": "19cc940e7a0ea0c909f140fc0bc79d19220cddd2",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T23:18:16Z",
      "body": "F11 constructs unresolved package/part reference syntax, but local reference chains had no separate linking result. This bounded linker resolves the actual parser's TypeReference parts through local declaration scopes, preserving found prefixes and wrong-type candidates while keeping syntax unchanged. Later qualified segments search only the prior resolved local scope; alias cycles, ambiguous names and unresolved targets remain explicit outcomes.\n\nAliases are caller-supplied visible-local observations because F11 does not parse alias syntax. Semantic results require an explicit declaration-to-local-JSON-node UUID association through the actual F04 registry. Resource, node and semantic IDs remain separate, with no fallback from syntax or semantic IDs. Private snapshot identities reject foreign result replay. Imports, native visibility/caches, inherited scopes, global libraries and reference assignment remain outside this finite family.\n\nValidation: 15 Rust integration tests, formatting and all-target Clippy pass offline/locked against unchanged inputs. The exact coordinator runner, six original streams, source hashes and executed linker/test bytes are retained. Static source checks pin the candidate Syside linker/scope/naming/reference metadata and exact F11/F04 implementations; no upstream/native oracle was run. This PR targets the exact F04/F11 dependency snapshot. Land prerequisites first, then retarget and revalidate; never merge into the snapshot branch.\n\nIndependent read-only review found no blocking issue within the documented finite family. That review is separate from the coordinator's executed checks.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 49,
      "title": "F46: Expose scoped semantic owners and selected effective names",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/49",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f46",
      "head_sha": "1cf521c107eabd75aeec658264017bf72b381b0b",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-base-f46-20261025",
      "base_sha": "78aa06f55abc10d6f60280a9d9d301f0ad6b66ef",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T23:17:43Z",
      "body": "Semantic owner/name operations needed an explicit immutable resource binding. This standalone adapter exposes actual owner and ordered ownedElement flattening, effective primary/short names and the current qualified-name policy. It calls the existing ResourceSet owner adapter and F04 reference registry, preserving resource/snapshot identity and refusing foreign handles, unresolved references, wrong types, unsupported wire forms and naming cycles.\n\nFeature inheritance uses the first Redefinition only when both declared names are absent. Empty primary names and short-only declarations preserve their native distinction; qualified names use the printable-name helper and semantic membership-owner skip. Selected cross-resource library inheritance retains the object's local owner. F03 remains a frozen prerequisite boundary; these actual Element getters do not call import evaluation, so no artificial import-query binding is introduced.\n\nValidation:14 Rust integration tests, formatting, scoped all-target Clippy and11 source pins pass. The exact coordinator runner, six raw streams and unchanged hashes for all65 captured inputs are retained. Parent source review found no blocking issue within this finite getter family. The inherited initializer emits its existing atomic deprecation warning; its source is unchanged and scoped Clippy exits0. No native Java/EMF runtime was executed.\n\nThis PR targets the exact F03/F04 prerequisite snapshot; land prerequisites, then retarget and revalidate. Never merge into the snapshot branch. A separate crate preserves the held initializer-graph source/tests. Proxy loading, graph mutation, cache/inverse notifications, malformed Java UTF-16, all derived operations and full native parity remain outside scope.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 48,
      "title": "F01: Bind GeneralView planning to resource-scoped query snapshots",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/48",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f01",
      "head_sha": "ffe50e7f53acef1263167388454f22452f08dda1",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T22:50:15Z",
      "body": "GeneralView lookup returned resource-scoped query results, but ViewUsage planning had no safe binding for them. This standalone adapter runs the existing initializer planner, obtains an immutable observation at the actual query prefix, and replaces its temporary GeneralView handle with a typed target carrying resource and snapshot identity. Other local planning steps retain their source order; mismatched prefix/context and unresolved input stay incomplete.\n\nDetached context, a resource without a set and ordinary no-match remain distinct known-absence results. Equal semantic IDs in separate resources follow the existing ordered query, and an identical-byte replacement snapshot cannot authorize old targets. Delegated external handles cannot alias the temporary query symbol; no unqualified GeneralView handle or legacy plan escapes.\n\nValidation: 12 Rust tests, formatting, all-target Clippy and five exact upstream/adapter source pins pass. Exact runners, executed source hashes and raw streams are retained. The first capture passed 11 tests and failed a dispatch-trace fixture that incorrectly used a source-method name; its original inputs/output remain preserved. The passing capture also uses the installed atomic try_update API in this new crate. The inherited initializer still emits its existing fetch_update deprecation warning; its source is unchanged and scoped Clippy exits0.\n\nThe snapshot provider asserts resource visibility for the exact planner prefix; this association does not attest native correspondence. Graph application, ViewUsage mutation, external-reference assignment, native import evaluation and URI loading remain outside scope. The adapter preserves the older held graph paths by using a separate crate; the frozen F01 brief's proposed write paths are adjusted accordingly. No upstream runtime or production operation ran.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 47,
      "title": "F04: Resolve selected EMF references in immutable explicit resources",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/47",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f04",
      "head_sha": "034670a48296ba154e7fea3ddaa9f0f5524f008b",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T22:47:21Z",
      "body": "Local JSON node ids and library semantic elementIds cannot be resolved interchangeably. This standalone adapter decodes the pinned selected reference family and resolves it against immutable caller-supplied Documents, retaining resource key, JSON node id and semantic elementId separately. Bare UUIDs use local node identity; selected library fragments use an explicit per-resource identity policy. Class prefixes and expected types both use real metamodel assignability. Invalid, unsupported, absent, unresolved, wrong-type and stale-snapshot outcomes remain distinct.\n\nTargets carry a private process-local snapshot token and are rejected by another registry, even for identical documents. No URI, network, filesystem or database loading occurs. Actual pinned Batmobile and StandardViewDefinitions objects exercise identity distinctions; synthetic registry URI keys are explicitly labeled. This crate avoids existing held initializer-graph source/tests, with no shared module or manifest changes.\n\nValidation:16 Rust integration tests, formatting, all-target Clippy and seven source pins/four native identity examples pass. The exact coordinator runner, original streams and unchanged-input hashes include both native JSON fixture files. Upstream/native EMF execution was not run. The original graph binding, ordinary resource schemes, relative/percent/path/proxy forms, migration, reference-chain evaluation and full EMF/SysON parity remain excluded. No new registry dependency or production action is introduced.\n\nIndependent source-only review of the frozen resolver/tests found no blocking issue within the documented selected family; that review is separate from the coordinator's executed checks.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 46,
      "title": "F21: Pin session and project-isolation contracts and qualification blockers",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/46",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f21",
      "head_sha": "ebc14e80f773e608e877dd93f7034d413a8da5b4",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T22:45:45Z",
      "body": "API parity work needs an explicit session/project boundary before selecting a Rust host adapter. This PR records the pinned SysON dependency, configuration and delegate chain, with 18 source-file pins and twelve unrun negative scenarios covering identity, project context, session/cookie, CSRF, HTTP/WS origins and source/artifact correspondence.\n\nThe security manual's no-built-in-auth statement, inherited Sirius Web starter/client boundaries, explicit CORS declarations and object/library read-only behavior retain their exact scopes. No deployed JAR/image or effective policy is bound. Native outcomes and host selection remain unresolved; the packet's qualification is BLOCKED_SOURCE_PREPARATION_ONLY.\n\nValidation: 21 stdlib regression tests and the 18-pin source/12-scenario checker pass, with original runner, stdout/stderr and unchanged-input hashes retained. Checks reject source drift, missing negative families and false runtime/acceptance promotion. No HTTP request, upstream lifecycle, database, credential or policy change ran. The packet supplies reviewed preparation for later API/command work, with operational security and native behavior still unqualified.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 45,
      "title": "F19C: Bind measured canvas layout and routing to the WASM editor",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/45",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f19",
      "head_sha": "797b1c194b1cd46f0152b257d337e6cf2983041c",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f19-controller",
      "base_sha": "00c3eee7eb8cdc16c37daeb6589a4767ea37aa29",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T22:17:49Z",
      "body": "The model editor previously used linear preview positions and an isolated dimension swap. Layout canvas now measures the rendered name-label style, runs the real F19A package/part layout and routing through the F19B ticket controller, and publishes computed node geometry and typing routes. Rotate preview uses the same pipeline and retains unselected geometry; full layout resizes package containers afterward.\n\nThe browser awaits fonts, rejects stale model/selection/font generations, queues compute and apply separately, and preserves editable drafts, focus, caret and open details during canvas requests/background publication. Separate Canvas undo/redo and a model-bound geometry JSON companion leave semantic model history/export unchanged. View bounds include every node and route point, including outside/negative imported routes. Existing authoring/scalar assertions remain intact; their added guards block service workers and external requests.\n\nValidation:40 Rust tests, formatting, all-target Clippy, release WASM and all three actual browser journeys pass against unchanged captured inputs. The new deterministic-clock journey checks cancellation/stale publication, drafts, simulated font-generation invalidation, rotation/incident edges, history, atomic import, viewport fit and same-byte model-import invalidation. Layout console errors/warnings are empty. The coordinator inspected desktop/mobile canvas captures. Exact runners, streams, source/WASM linkage and geometry output are retained; screenshots stay outside the repository. An initial artifact-directory setup failed before any server/browser and is preserved separately.\n\nThis finite package/part canvas depends on the F19A geometry and F19B controller PRs; land prerequisites, then retarget and revalidate. Unsupported classes, ports, cross-parent typing and container rotation fail explicitly. Imported geometry is validated file data, not a fresh measurement or native runtime/ELK parity claim. No held graph path, production service or new browser dependency is changed.\n\n\nDepends on [F19B #44](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/44), following [F19A #43](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/43).",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 44,
      "title": "F19B: Add cooperative canvas requests, history and geometry persistence",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/44",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f19-controller",
      "head_sha": "00c3eee7eb8cdc16c37daeb6589a4767ea37aa29",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f19-geometry",
      "base_sha": "216d4cb5004120a90fc4b85c48dbd4a3c40e959d",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T22:18:23Z",
      "body": "The canvas geometry composition has no request lifecycle, publication boundary or persisted history. This controller adds cooperative prepare/compute/apply tickets, separate canvas undo/redo and model-bound companion geometry JSON over the real F19A computation. Cancelled or superseded requests cannot publish; model changes invalidate history, and scene reads/export/history reject another committed model.\n\nImport derives node, parent and typing identity directly from the bound semantic document. Strict fields, integer nodes/header data, half-unit orthogonal route endpoints and duplicate/unknown IDs are validated before any state change. A shared encoder bounds both the canonical file and its escaped default-ABI envelope before publication, so exported admitted scenes can be reimported within the same byte budget. Model bytes remain unchanged. Imported geometry is file data, not a fresh measurement or computed-layout attestation.\n\nValidation:40 Rust tests pass (11 controller,9 inherited geometry,20 inherited web), formatting, all-target Clippy and3 prerequisite source checks pass. Exact coordinator runner, raw streams, input hashes and unchanged-input receipt are retained. Browser and upstream-runtime execution are outside this controller stage.\n\nThis PR depends on the immutable F19A geometry stage and precedes the rendered App/loader stage. Land prerequisites first, then retarget and revalidate. It changes no App actions, browser loader, held graph path or production service.\n\n\nDepends on [F19A #43](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/43); rendered binding follows as F19C.\n\nRendered binding is now available as [F19C #45](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/45).",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 43,
      "title": "Compose measured package geometry and orthogonal routes",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/43",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f19-geometry",
      "head_sha": "216d4cb5004120a90fc4b85c48dbd4a3c40e959d",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-base-f19-20261025",
      "base_sha": "a312510b19dd69eb0582043c5edb6829aac7da15",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T22:18:20Z",
      "body": "The web crate has no computed package/part canvas geometry API. This first F19 stage composes real F15 leaf sizing, F18 package forests and F17 sibling routing while preserving the committed semantic document. It accepts a finite package/part family, explicit name-label observations and same-parent typing edges; unsupported model classes, ports, identities and geometry fail explicitly.\n\nThe owning container is excluded from its child router, while sibling containers remain obstacles. Leaf rotation computations retain unselected endpoint positions. Whole-pixel measurement/header policy and part rectangle sizing are proposed canvas policies, not native rendering or ELK parity. Existing route buffers are recomputed without copying them.\n\nValidation: 29 Rust tests pass (9 new geometry tests and 20 existing web tests), plus formatting, all-target Clippy and five pinned prerequisite source checks. Original compile, fixture-assumption and lint failures retain exact source/streams/runners alongside the final passing capture. No browser or upstream runtime ran in this stage.\n\nThis PR is the first of three ordered F19 stages; controller and actual rendered binding follow as separate dependent PRs in this batch. It targets the immutable F15/F17/F18 snapshot. Land prerequisites first, then retarget and revalidate; never merge into the snapshot branch. No App/loader binding or held graph path is changed here.\n\n\nF19 review chain: [geometry #43](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/43) \u2192 [controller #44](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/44) \u2192 [rendered WASM binding #45](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/45).",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 42,
      "title": "Prepare immutable upstream build and launch preflight",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/42",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f39",
      "head_sha": "fa85317782c535217d5a937178fdce2167bb92cf",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T21:41:25Z",
      "body": "The reference lane had source inventories but no checked immutable build/launch\npreflight. This adds a source-only packet that pins 13 Git inputs, extracts the\nsource lifecycle/tool requirements, records bounded installed-tool observations,\nand freezes structured review-only command templates plus synthetic paths/ports,\nstop conditions and retention rules.\n\nThe checker separates a passing preparation check from execution readiness:\nexecution remains BLOCKED. The selected Java/Node versions and observed Node\nalternatives do not establish the exact source toolchain. npm package metadata\nis distinct from CLI qualification; registry entitlement was not probed. Effective\nMaven/npm artifacts, the EMF JSON SNAPSHOT/source correspondence, curated build\nenvironment, synthetic DB and fresh destinations remain unresolved. Vite's\nprocess.env/loadEnv inputs are recorded as a required environment-review boundary.\n\nValidation: 21 stdlib-only synthetic tests and 13 source pins pass. Exact version\ncommand outputs, actual timestamps, executable hashes, source/runner hashes and\nraw checker/test streams are retained. Hashes of executable files do not claim\nwhole-distribution closure. No Maven/npm lifecycle, registry/network probe, build, server,\ndatabase, installation, credential-file read or production action was performed.\n\nThe future npm ci step is explicitly project dependency installation, even with\noffline/scripts-disabled flags; no such installation ran. System tool/package\nbaseline installation remains outside the proposed action. The original pre-review\n20-test packet and its five exact inputs are preserved beside the corrected capture.\n\nF39 has no future-unit prerequisites and targets rust/integration. F40 still\nrequires a separately reviewed, bound action; command templates are not runnable\nwhile their tool/config/artifact bindings remain unresolved. No merge is included.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 41,
      "title": "Apply structural operator-expression postprocessing",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/41",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f12",
      "head_sha": "25acfaa6f3059685f133be034355f11104aad16f",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-base-f12-20261025",
      "base_sha": "1d50b6f988a5ee8847f61a4c76e1d46766bad3a0",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T21:41:21Z",
      "body": "The AST adapter had no operation applying the retained OperatorExpression\npostprocessor. This adds structural postprocessing on synthetic kernel nodes:\nfalsey operands normalize to an empty array, and an empty array with one of the\nfour exact classification operators gets the source-shaped three-node implicit\nfeature-reference chain. Existing unary/binary/nested operand order is preserved;\nrepeated application is idempotent.\n\nF09's actual registry selects only this handler. A kernel transaction rolls back\nstructural writes and new nodes on failure, while spent IDs/work retain the\nkernel policy. Native child-cache aliases and immediate parent mutation remain\nunsupported; structural parenting finalizes through the immutable kernel arena.\nThis is not an expression-text parser or execution of the other four callbacks.\n\nValidation: 25 tests pass (12 new operator tests and 13 inherited F11), plus\nformatting and all-target Clippy offline/locked. Three retained source documents,\n19 associated static obligation tuples, 38 executed input hashes and original\nstreams/runner are recorded. Those tuples are not classification grammar\ncoverage; F08's ancestor-order qualification and upstream-runtime limits remain.\n\nThe PR targets the frozen F09/F11 prerequisite snapshot. Land both prerequisites\n(#35 and #40) before retargeting to integration, inspecting the new diff and\nrunning appropriate checks. Never merge into the snapshot branch. No held writer\npath, package baseline, service or integration branch is changed.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 40,
      "title": "Construct finite package and part ASTs from text",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/40",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f11",
      "head_sha": "ca1c4b3ab364db7dc9da835c66cba72912c3417f",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-base-f11-20261025",
      "base_sha": "2af6bfbc46b3c30ba7ccf0a2774d65c1ce578cc2",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T21:11:39Z",
      "body": "The parser foundation had reflection, primitive conversion and transactional AST\noperations but no adapter constructing package/part declarations from text. This\nadds a finite frontend for packages, part definitions and named typed part usages,\nwith source-shaped membership wrappers, raw primitive lexemes, byte/UTF-16 spans,\nmandatory defaults and immutable kernel parenting. Qualified references stay\nunresolved; final TypeReference markers use F08's positional type expectation.\n\nThe whitelist is explicit. Package/root usages use OwningMembership while usages\ninside part-definition bodies use FeatureMembership. Valid source outside the\nfamily returns Unsupported; malformed finite input returns a position. The\nadapter does not perform full grammar recognition/recovery, native resource import,\nsemantic linking, callback application or child-cache behavior. F08's ordering\nqualification remains an unqualified source-derived candidate.\n\nValidation: thirteen tests, formatting and all-target Clippy pass offline/locked.\nFour retained source documents, 14 selected obligations of 848 and 170 conservative\nkeyword exclusions pass source/hash checks. The original capture passed all 13\ntests but failed two style lints; exact failed source/streams/runner are retained,\nand the final capture passes after two expression-form refactors. The initial\nzero-keyword preparation correction is also recorded without invented evidence.\nNo native runtime or AST differential golden was executed.\n\nThis PR targets the immutable F08+F10 dependency snapshot. Land both prerequisites\nfirst, then retarget to merged integration, inspect the resulting diff and rerun\nappropriate checks. Do not merge this child into the snapshot branch. No parent\nsource, shared manifest, held writer path, backlog, package baseline or service\nis changed.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 38,
      "title": "Freeze candidate schema and migration declaration contracts",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/38",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f26",
      "head_sha": "fc15b4bdd4363af8e29ea5a842981bb21378a497",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T21:06:35Z",
      "body": "The existing DB inventory retained schema XML but did not freeze a checked declaration\nsequence. This adds a source-only planner for the captured candidate graph: 29 XML\ndocuments, 28 ordered includes and 20 changeSet file/id/author identities. Operations,\nattributes and character data are retained without computing an applied schema.\n\nThe planner rejects unsupported include/property/logical-identity forms, cycles,\nmissing/duplicate inputs and unclosed external payload/custom execution. DBMS,\nprecondition, rollback, transaction and checksum declarations remain unevaluated.\nSHA-256 source pins are explicitly separate from Liquibase history/checksums.\nA synthetic two-changeSet example and blocked separate-review command templates\nprepare the next execution decision without inventing unresolved tool/artifact bindings.\n\nValidation: 19 stdlib-only tests and four pinned integration Git inputs pass;\nraw outputs, exact runners/input hashes and original pre-fix capture are preserved.\nRoot review requested XML tail preservation and nonempty-include rejection; both\nhave regressions. Candidate-to-resolved-artifact correspondence remains UNPROVEN,\nincluding the EMF JSON SNAPSHOT. No database, migration, upstream lifecycle,\ndownload, service, credential, shared backlog or dependency change was performed.\n\nF26 has no future-unit prerequisites and targets rust/integration. This is a bounded\nsource-contract candidate, not resolved schema or whole DB parity.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 37,
      "title": "Evaluate public namespace imports on immutable snapshots",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/37",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f03",
      "head_sha": "1fd1ea5a45240a6c078620e6ac4b3cf25e67071e",
      "base_ref": "codex/syson-f02",
      "base_sha": "15501a5ff2459cd1056809b70f23d0d2ae895b8a",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-25T20:23:29Z",
      "body": "The public-import contract now has a bounded Rust evaluator on immutable caller\nobservations. It preserves ordered public traversal, exclusions, per-helper\nvisited state, alias reference observations and lazy name-conflict reads.\nSupplied import-result mode remains distinct from graph traversal. Reached\nunsupported or unresolved data returns explicit errors without partial success.\n\nThe implementation preserves a source-context quirk: nested helper dispatch\nreturns empty for Base Import; the direct API's null is represented by a Rust\nnull disposition, while an outer Namespace pipeline cannot flatten that null.\nNative bindings, proxies, Type/includeAll families and URI loading are excluded.\nThe standalone crate avoids the existing held graph-adapter paths.\n\nValidation: 15 tests pass, including replay of the actual 19 F02 fixture cases\nin one test (18 original expected dispositions plus one explicit unsupported\nincludeAll case), formatting and all-target Clippy. Source, stream and runner\nhashes are retained. Expectations are manually source-derived, not Java/EMF\nruntime goldens. No upstream runtime comparison or whole-area parity is claimed.\n\nStacked on F02 / PR #34 at `15501a5ff2459cd1056809b70f23d0d2ae895b8a`.\nMerge/review prerequisite first; after it lands, retarget this PR to the merged\nintegration base and inspect/revalidate the resulting diff. Do not merge into\nthe temporary prerequisite branch. No merge or shared manifest change is included.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 34,
      "title": "Freeze namespace import and exclusion contracts",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/34",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f02",
      "head_sha": "15501a5ff2459cd1056809b70f23d0d2ae895b8a",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-24T21:28:45Z",
      "body": "Namespace imports need a frozen behavior contract before the F03 evaluator can\nbe implemented. This change pins six native metamodel source blobs and adds\n19 ordered synthetic cases covering import/exclusion order, conflict state,\nalias reference identity, cycles, visibility and unsupported outcomes. It retains\nthe generated membershipsOfVisibility null result explicitly.\n\nA stdlib-only checker validates source/fixture integrity, local filter transition\nchecks and trace consistency. Graph outputs remain manually source-derived;\nno import evaluator or upstream runtime ran. The similarly named services helper\nis outside this native API dispatch path.\n\nValidation: final captured checks pass six source pins, 19 fixture cases and\n17 checker tests, including mutation rejection. Original 18-case capture and all\nraw streams are preserved. Root source review accepted the final scope. No Rust,\nmanifest, backlog, existing lease, package or service change is included.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 33,
      "title": "Add immutable move-provider dispatch registry",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/33",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f38",
      "head_sha": "546604c2cf64bf07586964c5683c0030fc85bd56",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-24T21:26:51Z",
      "body": "The Rust port has no typed immutable dispatch planner for the move-element\nprovider category. This adds a dependency-free `syson-extensions` crate that\npreserves caller injection order and duplicate slots, selects the first observed\nmatching custom provider, and plans the default fallback when none matches or\nwhen the selected custom provider returns null. Non-null failure statuses and\nnullable messages are retained without trying another delegate.\n\nCapability observations are immutable caller-supplied data. Missing observations\nare errors only when reached; no provider code or model move executes. Six pinned\nupstream Git blobs define the source-derived rules; Rust label and packet-shape\nadmission policies are explicitly separate.\n\nValidation: 17 focused tests pass, including 511 exhaustive combinations in one\ntest, plus formatting, all-target Clippy with warnings denied, and source-pin\nchecks. Root source review and the nullable-message correction are recorded.\nOriginal run streams, executed runner/input hashes, and the initial source-range\nmetadata failure are preserved. Java/Spring runtime comparison, native capability\nadapters and whole-area extension parity remain unverified.\n\nF38 has no outstanding future-unit prerequisites. Base is `rust/integration` at\n`ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92`. No shared module/manifest/backlog\nwiring, package update or merge is included.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 32,
      "title": "Qualify local snapshot publication failures with deterministic I/O",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/32",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f31",
      "head_sha": "762217dd56e6a0c4cd2aa2a01bfb62454bb8b6e9",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-24T21:26:47Z",
      "body": "The local snapshot adapter previously had no deterministic way to exercise write, sync and publication failures. This change adds a trusted `SnapshotIo` seam while keeping `save_new` on the same shared implementation and standard-library operations. Existing errors and no-replace publication remain compatible.\n\nThirteen new real-filesystem tests preserve an unrelated original snapshot and inspect staged/final bytes through fresh stores. They cover partial writes, each operation boundary, existing-file collisions and errors after publication/removal. In particular, an `Io` error can accompany a readable published file; an after-removal error can leave no staging, and retry still cannot replace that file.\n\nValidation: coordinator-run full default workflow formatting, 15 tests (13 new, 2 existing) and all-target Clippy with warnings denied passed offline/locked with one compiler/test thread. Captured source remained unchanged. Original commands, streams, runner hashes, pinned baseline and retained-fixture inventory are included in `porting/follow-ons/F31`.\n\nThis is local snapshot failure qualification, not PostgreSQL recovery or crash/power-loss/upstream parity. Candidate factory feature and non-Unix execution remain unrun. No dependencies, manifests, services, automatic cleanup or recovery policy change.\n",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 31,
      "title": "F45: generate resource-dependent identities and preserve selected ID roles",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/31",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f45",
      "head_sha": "7200b3c7583e6c3bd7a474030344323e3fcb93e2",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-24T20:53:15Z",
      "body": "Adds source-derived UUID decisions over explicit resource/library/name observations, preserving eager fresh-v4 provider consumption before deterministic UUIDv5 branches and lazy null/unresolved outcomes. Semantic and resource identities remain distinct typed roles. A separately labeled proposed selected-document reservation facility checks both collision roles before mutation.\n\nValidation: 18 new identity cases plus28 existing domain/query regressions pass; one actual Document/Editor/immutable SnapshotStore integration case imports11 fixture objects, commits distinct selected IDs, cancels/refuses collisions without changing saved bytes, then reloads through a fresh store. Formatting, clippy warnings denied, nine pinned source checks and coordinator review pass. All executed input hashes match this commit.\n\nThe initial integration attempt stopped before tests because the new harness's manually copied lock required default-feature pruning. The original refused lock/runner/streams are retained; offline regeneration removed only two inactive local initializer packages and adjusted the local workflow row, leaving every registry package record unchanged. The final locked integration passes. See porting/follow-ons/F45 and porting/domain/identity-context.\n\nCanonical UUID spelling and immutable observation restrictions are explicit; no automatic random substitution, proxy loading, complete native identity adapter, crash recovery or upstream runtime parity is claimed. Implements independent F45 from PR #22, targeting rust/integration. Keep draft; no merge or deployment.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 30,
      "title": "F20: freeze REST read DTO and serializer contracts",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/30",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f20",
      "head_sha": "53dffb79ede9ee05464c75e037b8b74a3db8319c",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-24T20:53:12Z",
      "body": "Adds typed adapters for the selected element-by-ID and relationships read contracts, validated JSON that retains original wire text, caller-observed SysML serializer decisions and relationship/traversal projection. Known controller200/404 branches preserve bare HTTP bodies, empty relationship success and default BOTH direction; unresolved binding/authentication/dispatch failures stay explicit.\n\nThe serializer observations retain null/enum/reference distinctions, UTF16 feature-name ordering, single-vs-many library filtering and exact eAnnotations identity omission. Relationship results are explicitly unordered; implied relationship omission does not prune descendants. serde_json is pinned to the existing1.0.151/arbitrary_precision inputs, with raw number spelling kept separate from structural Value views.\n\nValidation: 21 tests, formatting, clippy warnings denied, source/hash checks and coordinator source review pass. Two original upstream JSON expectations remain source fixtures, not runtime goldens. Committed crate inputs exactly match the passing freeze in porting/follow-ons/F20. No server, native getter adapter, HTTP/Jackson runtime comparison or authorization implementation is claimed.\n\nImplements independent F20 from PR #22. Targets rust/integration; the actual read server and session/isolation work remain separate dependencies. Keep draft; no merge or deployment.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 28,
      "title": "F43: verify Rust/WASM distribution graph and notice inputs",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/28",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f43",
      "head_sha": "ae763874c419cd16ebf8e426ce6859ac97ffb101",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-24T21:07:37Z",
      "body": "Adds stdlib-only verification of a supplied Rust/WASM source bundle against reviewed policy and actual offline/locked default/candidate Cargo metadata captures. It checks active normal dependency edges, source/lock/profile identity, packaged source/notices/licenses/manifests and locked archive checksums, rejecting missing/altered files, unknown dependencies, symlinks and extra payloads.\n\nTest fixtures materialize and hash-check the policy-pinned Git snapshot in their own workspace directory, so independent source edits do not invalidate the fixtures. The production verifier still rejects supplied source that differs from its fixed policy. The builder uses existing admitted archives and an explicitly synthetic empty WASM module; build correspondence and full legal clearance remain unproven.\n\nValidation: the corrected 19 tests pass in a synthetic source composition of all nine implementation PRs. The combined F44/F45 domain also passes62 tests and clippy. Original individual captures, the reproduced pre-fix setup failure, and the corrected composition result are retained; the reproduction's missing execution UTC is explicit. Optimized Python reproduces six policy/manifest files and rejects a wrong source pin. No build, download, archive extraction, installation, upstream runtime or Git merge occurred.\n\nSee porting/follow-ons/F43/VALIDATION.json, REVIEW.md and TEST-ISOLATION.md for exact inputs, captures and limits. Implements independent F43 from PR #22, targeting rust/integration. Keep draft; no merge or deployment.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 26,
      "title": "F44: qualify Unicode naming and alias identity boundaries",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/26",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f44",
      "head_sha": "4160e7566f0ca250669e2e44aeeda15a9be0e200",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-24T20:24:38Z",
      "body": "Adds 16 source-derived regression cases for Java whitespace stripping, quote timing/asymmetry, UTF-16 escaping, literal qualified-name splitting and alias reference identity. Existing names.rs remains unchanged because the source audit established no supported-domain executable divergence.\n\nValidation: all 16 new cases and 28 existing domain/query regressions pass, with changed-file formatting, clippy warnings denied and coordinator source review. Six pinned source hashes reproduce. Exact receipts, logs, primary source links and input dispositions are in porting/domain/name-unicode and porting/follow-ons/F44. All captured crate bytes match the commit; one exact-file attribute preserves original stdout.\n\nJava isolated-surrogate inputs, native alias-adapter observations and upstream runtime comparison remain unqualified. This qualifies the stated scalar-string contract rather than complete naming or semantic parity. Implements independent F44 from PR #22; targets rust/integration. Keep draft; no merge or deployment.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 25,
      "title": "F10: convert AST primitive values without losing source spelling",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/25",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f10",
      "head_sha": "48ee69e41c4f29346f1d95075278d84aefc48057",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-24T20:12:18Z",
      "body": "Adds a standalone Rust primitive-conversion layer with explicit undefined/null/value states, source spans and raw lexeme retention. It preserves UTF-16 slicing and quote/escape behavior, separates later name sanitation, and handles decimal/radix binary64 conversion, signed zero, nonfinite values and raw-spelling integer/rational classification.\n\nRule-name dispatch precedes declared type, so STRING_VALUE and UNRESTRICTED_NAME keep their quotes at this layer. BigInt/Date helper routes and non-ASCII dispatch names are explicitly unsupported; this does not parse, link, serialize full ASTs or import semantic models.\n\nValidation: 16 focused tests, formatting and clippy with warnings denied pass; pinned-source hash checks and coordinator source review passed. The empty-name output-budget boundary is covered by 0/1/2-unit and cancellation cases. Original receipts/source hashes are in porting/follow-ons/F10; all captured crate bytes match this commit. Two exact-file whitespace rules preserve supplied notice and transcript bytes and postdate the runtime freeze. No upstream parser/runtime comparison ran.\n\nImplements planned F10 from PR #22. Targets rust/integration independently of F08/F25. Keep draft; no merge or deployment.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 24,
      "title": "F25: plan document reconciliation with explicit identity and mutation admission",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/24",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f25",
      "head_sha": "b454d4991d2518dd58ecab29ddcffe012823c46d",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-24T20:10:30Z",
      "body": "Adds a standalone pure Rust planner for the pinned Sirius document/dependency reconciliation contracts. It preserves object identity separately from UUID, first-existing matching, duplicate-UUID behavior, timestamp/readOnly defaults, unchanged collection/domain behavior and ordered caller effect requests. Dependency operations require explicit mutation admission and supplied wrapper equality.\n\nThe planner performs no database write, clock/UUID allocation or event publication. Null/malformed Java objects and collection implementation behavior outside the admitted typed inputs remain unsupported; resolved deployed-artifact correspondence and upstream runtime parity remain open.\n\nValidation: 15 focused tests, formatting and clippy with warnings denied pass. Coordinator source review and exact committed-versus-executed source checks passed. The original E0308 implementation compile failure and E0716 test compile failure are preserved alongside the final passing capture in porting/follow-ons/F25. Exact original stdout is retained through one exact-path whitespace rule. No database or upstream application ran.\n\nImplements planned F25 from PR #22. Targets rust/integration; no dependent follow-on is required. Keep draft; no merge or deployment.",
      "labels": []
    },
    {
      "number": 23,
      "title": "F08: add immutable AST reflection tables and checked handles",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/23",
      "head_ref": "codex/syson-f08",
      "head_sha": "7d1eb8a1a05c292c78ca27482158c6dfe5196c3b",
      "base_ref": "rust/integration",
      "base_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-24T20:10:26Z",
      "body": "Adds a standalone Rust reflection database for the 189 retained Syside AST names, ordered ancestor/subtype tables, effective mandatory-property metadata and checked reference-position typing. Handles retain table ownership and reject foreign-table use; unknown names and invalid positions are explicit errors.\n\nThe subtype comparator does not define a strict weak order. The public API exposes the chosen short-sort order as a source-derived candidate, and retained partitions/four literal source expectations document its limits. This does not implement AST construction, linking, semantic validation or verified original JavaScript ordering.\n\nValidation: eight focused tests pass, including all 189 source tables and 35,721 subtype assertions; formatting, clippy with warnings denied, source-generation checks and coordinator source review passed. Original coordinator receipts/streams and source hashes are in porting/follow-ons/F08. Committed crate bytes match the executed freeze; transcript bytes are preserved through one exact-path whitespace rule. No upstream runtime comparison ran.\n\nImplements planned F08 from PR #22. Targets rust/integration; no dependent follow-on is required. Keep draft; no merge or deployment.",
      "labels": []
    },
