      "base_sha": "a5c87ec50b542fc550c54486743ba9320994f1fa",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-24T19:35:23Z",
      "body": "Final model delta: factory candidate, containment, selected scalar admission and PortDefinition reference API. Independent factory acceptance remains pending.\n\nExtracted from [the preserved integration rollup](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/1) at `ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92`. 36 changed files; 9026 lines in source/script files, including declarative tables and tests. Large JSON/JSONL and stored run outputs are immutable evidence, not new feature counts. \n\nDependencies:\nS07 https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/8\n\nReview scope: `porting/area-inventories`, `porting/domain`, `rust/crates/syson-model`.\n\nIntegration: stacked on its prerequisite branch. Retarget to main after that prerequisite lands. Keep draft; no merge is authorized. Review can proceed in parallel, but shared compiler slots and held ownership leases still require coordination.\n\nValidation: a stdlib-only structural checker reconstructed the original final Git tree exactly (paths, modes and blob IDs), checked 102 path dependency references and 68 literal included-file references across the split heads. No Rust, browser or upstream application test was rerun for these new commits. Existing receipts retain their original executed revisions and limits; they are not relabeled as acceptance of this branch. Full-area parity remains unverified.\n\nSelf-review: the change is a source-preserving extraction. No upstream product release note is claimed; this is draft Rust port work. Existing licenses, failure evidence, default-off candidate gates and independent-review gaps remain in scope.",
      "labels": []
