    {
      "number": 1,
      "title": "Rust port integration rollup (review split into #2\u2013#21)",
      "draft": true,
      "url": "https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/1",
      "head_ref": "rust/integration",
      "head_sha": "ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92",
      "base_ref": "main",
      "base_sha": "6ba2ac64e6b16ee2b05752ad55395eebb87d4910",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-24T19:47:02Z",
      "body": "**Review split:** the implementation is now available as 20 component draft PRs, #2\u2013#21. [PR #22](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/pull/22) contains the [component index, dependency/retargeting instructions and 47 follow-on PR briefs](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/blob/79ef6b217fa4d6e33d019d63cbf509072a814224/porting/pr-split-20261024/README.md).\n\nThis PR preserves the original integration history and evidence. Review the component PRs; do not merge both this rollup and its duplicate component sequence. Temporary dependency bases are review snapshots: retarget dependents to main after prerequisites land. The 47 future units remain planned, not implemented. Existing held leases and execution gates remain authoritative.\n\n---\n\nIncrementally ports SysON to Rust: domain/metamodel foundations, transactional selected JSON edits, initialized construction in a Rust/WASM editor, and grammar/CST/AST kernels. Full application parity remains incomplete. Pinned upstream is `6ba2ac64e6b16ee2b05752ad55395eebb87d4910`; original licenses/notices are retained.\n\nThe query engine now accepts separate raw containment, semantic owned elements, effective names, physical-container state and public-import observations. Existing Model lookup delegates to the same algorithm. The native selected-JSON adapter adds immutable ordered ResourceSet snapshots and resource-scoped results, preserves first-name/type/import precedence, resolves local Feature and conjugated-Port effective names, and distinguishes known no-ResourceSet absence from unresolved claimed members or references. GeneralView lookup uses the pinned qualified name and type; native import computation, URI/proxy loading, NativeContext binding and ViewUsage mutation remain explicit gaps.\n\nThe editor's earlier opt-in ConnectionDefinition, InterfaceDefinition, AcceptActionUsage and PortDefinition workflow remains in place, with initialized children, staging/cancellation, one commit/undo/redo and selected JSON reload. Its raw-factory candidate stays disabled by default. [Authoring checkpoint](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/blob/ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92/porting/restarts/2026-10-24/README.md).\n\nCurrent query validation:\n- **26 new source-derived query cases**: 8 shared-engine and 18 adapter cases. Pinned ElementUtilTest contains UUID tests; these are synthetic cases derived from pinned query/getter source, not upstream runtime tests.\n- Fresh offline/locked runs passed **56 focused, 245 regression and 31 downstream test executions**, including repeated cases across runs. Default and candidate WASM builds passed; no final source drift or timeout.\n- Tests cover raw versus semantic traversal, all-Relationship flattening, resource/root order, scoped identity, absence/errors, lazy imports/getters, invalid containment/unknown classes, references/proxies/cycles, GeneralView and generated PortDefinition serialize/reload \u2192 conjugated `~Power` lookup.\n- The original focused failure is preserved: the generated-Port fixture used the restricted legacy rename API; it was corrected to use the existing generic attribute path. Independent review also found and resolved empty invalid-containment admission before the passing capture.\n- Separate workers implemented the shared engine and independent tests; an independent reviewer checked corrected source, exact pinned hashes, actual receipts/current source hashes and the public package. Reviewer runtime execution was not claimed. No registry versions/checksums changed.\n\nSee [query contract and qualification](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/blob/ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92/porting/domain/native-query/README.md), [source provenance](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/blob/ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92/porting/domain/native-query/PROVENANCE.json), [qualification/receipt index](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/blob/ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92/porting/domain/native-query/QUALIFICATION.json), and [parity ledger](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/blob/ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92/porting/PARITY-LEDGER.json). Both original dirty working ledgers, their held query inventory/validator leases and unpublished evidence remain preserved; no historical frozen gate was replayed.\n\n**Implemented, locally tested and upstream-parity-verified remain separate.** Upstream application runtime comparison is NOT_RUN, zero complete areas are parity verified, and the unchanged 18-area inventory remains incomplete. Selected JSON snapshots and caller-supplied import observations do not establish full EMF caches/eIsSet/notifications/inverses/proxies, native import/ResourceSet equivalence, full serialization, broad semantics, layout/edges, API/database/collaboration, recovery, interchange, accessibility or user acceptance.\n\nThe [oracle decision](https://github.com/ajhcs/syson/blob/ad814c232ee24109639c1d52239cbeec6f4a3e92/porting/ORACLE-DECISION.md) still has unresolved toolchain, SNAPSHOT artifact/package-entitlement, lifecycle review and isolated synthetic database/runtime launch gates. No upstream application was launched. Next work is a resource-scoped GeneralView planner binding and the ViewUsage reference/application contract, preserving prefix visibility and snapshot identity.\n\nKeep draft. No merge or deployment.",
      "labels": []
    }
  ]
